# ---- Lineage 29, box 1: the kinds of obstacle (G189) ----
backlog:Imp_RuleRefusal a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ImpedimentKind ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Refusal by a rule"@en ;
    skos:definition "A gate, shape, probe or tool refused the work as it was designed to, because an obligation of the discipline was not met at that step and nothing else caused it. Tie-break between kinds: the cause decides, not the way the obstacle was detected, so a refusal that follows from a tool at fault, a wrong order or a missing record is of that kind. Example: the link-control probe refused a predicate declared nowhere, thirty minutes into release 1.468.0."@en .
backlog:Imp_EvidenceGap a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ImpedimentKind ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence missing"@en ;
    skos:definition "A claim, figure or record could not be shown by evidence the reader can check. Example: a reviewer could not find the figure 44; a test drive lived in a scratch directory."@en .
backlog:Imp_ToolFault a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ImpedimentKind ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Tool at fault"@en ;
    skos:definition "A tool is wrong, stale or not yet built, so the step it serves cannot be done as designed. Example: the step tool looked for any kick-off, found the one of another lineage and recorded none."@en .
backlog:Imp_WrongOrder a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ImpedimentKind ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Work in the wrong order"@en ;
    skos:definition "The work was done before what it needs exists. Example: the Objective stage linked stories that the Backlog stage had not yet created."@en .
backlog:Imp_AccessLimit a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ImpedimentKind ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Resource out of reach"@en ;
    skos:definition "A page, file, register or permission the work needs is outside what the agent can reach. Example: GitHub folder pages cannot be fetched by the session; an objective counted lines in another session's register."@en .
backlog:Imp_DecisionWaiting a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ImpedimentKind ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Decision waited on"@en ;
    skos:definition "A decision only a person may take is not yet taken, and the rules and facts do not settle it. Example: the order of two lineages, put to the Owner on 2026-11-02."@en .
backlog:Imp_ServiceFailure a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ImpedimentKind ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Outside service failing"@en ;
    skos:definition "A service outside the package fails or hangs up though the work is right. Example: the push of a release tag answered 'the remote end hung up unexpectedly' in releases 3.0.0, 3.3.0 and 3.5.0."@en .
backlog:RS_ImpedimentsKnown a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:RuleSet ;
    rdfs:label "An impediment names its kind"@en ;
    skos:definition "Within an adopting lineage or register, every impediment names one of the seven kinds of obstacle. A RuleSet because it binds only an adopter; a lineage opened under an earlier revision is not bound."@en .
backlog:Pr_13 a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ProfileRevision ; rdfs:label "Profile revision 13"@en ; backlog:revisionNumber 13 ; skos:definition "Adds to the agentic adaptive profile (AAL) the rule set of known kinds of obstacle, so that a lineage opened under it records each impediment with its kind. The other profiles are not changed."@en .
backlog:Profile_AgenticAdaptive backlog:profileIncludes backlog:RS_ImpedimentsKnown .
backlog:RS_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:introducedInRevision backlog:Pr_13 .
fw:Ruling_G189 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G189" ;
    rdfs:label "An obstacle has a kind from a known set"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "An impediment of a lineage or register that adopts RS_ImpedimentsKnown names one of seven kinds of obstacle: a rule refused, evidence missing, a tool at fault, work in the wrong order, a resource out of reach, a decision waited on, an outside service failing. An impediment never names two kinds or a non-kind. The kinds were drawn from 29 classified findings (of 105) and from the sessions, and each of the 29 names one kind; where two kinds fit, the cause decides. AAL includes the rule set from profile revision 13; the other profiles are unchanged." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:ImpedimentKindShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "LINEAGE_OPERATING_DISCIPLINE v153.0.0, section G189; Owner direction of 2026-11-02 10:35." .
fw:Ruling_G189 backlog:rulingDecides backlog:RS_ImpedimentsKnown , backlog:Pr_13 , backlog:Profile_AgenticAdaptive .
# The kind of obstacle named by each of 29 classified findings whose root cause names a refusal, a failure or a wait.
fw:Find_MissingFixtureCaseName backlog:hasImpedimentKind backlog:Imp_RuleRefusal .
