# ---- Lineage 29: closure ----
fw:CR_ImpedimentsKnown a backlog:ClosureReport ;
    backlog:closesForMission fw:Mission_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:reportGeneratedAt "2026-11-02T18:34:25Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasClosureSummary "The mission asked that an obstacle that stops the work can be named, recorded and cleared. The Owner's direction of 2026-11-02 10:35 made three pieces of work, one box each, every box checked by fresh agents. Box 1: an obstacle has one of seven kinds (rule refused, evidence missing, tool at fault, wrong order, access limited, decision waited on, outside service failing), a shape refuses an impediment of an adopting lineage with no kind, 29 of the 105 findings were classified, and the profile gained a rule set (21 for the Adaptive-agentic profile); two reviews found a false scope claim, twelve misplaced findings and untested branches, partly repaired. Box 2: fourteen ways to clear an obstacle, each kind lists those that fit it, a cleared impediment names the way used and one its kind lists, a way with no time of resolution is refused; the first review removed two ways that clear nothing. Box 3: backlog_impediment raises, advises on and clears an obstacle, the agent monitor lists every open obstacle in hours with the ways that fit, the dates report names the obstacles that stood in a late box; four reviews found a tool that corrupted or lost data in six ways, all repaired and confirmed, and the real obstacle of the lineage was entered with it. Objectives at target: findings fitting no kind 30 to 0, kinds with no way listed 7 to 0, acts the tool cannot do 3 to 0, deliverables not satisfied 4 to 0, containment held. Not achieved: three findings remain in a kind they do not fit, evidence missing has no way that supplies the evidence and an outside service failing has only a retry, the other 76 findings were not read, no obstacle has yet been raised live, the shapes have not fired on real data because this lineage is not bound by them, the release preflight does not run the vocabulary probe, and the agent stays the grantor of the reviewers' access, an open gap against the Agentic-Systems rule that a person grants access. Unplanned: the date-plan tool was given an effort option before box 1, one catalogue shape and two coded rejections were added when the gate refused, and the outcome of the five objectives is recorded now (Retrospective) because their checkpoints of 2026-11-03 would otherwise fall due with no observation dated after them." ;
    backlog:reportsOnObjective fw:Obj_IK_MissionMet , fw:Obj_IK_Kind , fw:Obj_IK_Method , fw:Obj_IK_Record , fw:Obj_IK_Kept ;
    backlog:citesFinding fw:Find_IK_CatalogueGapsLeftAtClosure , fw:Find_IK_KindDatePlanPrerequisite , fw:Find_IK_KindFirstReviewDefects , fw:Find_IK_KindOldRecordsSayThirty , fw:Find_IK_KindThreePlacementsStillWrong , fw:Find_IK_KindUntestedBranches , fw:Find_IK_RealRecordEnteredAfterTheFact , fw:Find_IK_ReleasePreflightMissesVocabulary , fw:Find_IK_ToolAcceptedAndUnscoped , fw:Find_IK_ToolReviewRounds , fw:Find_IK_WaysEvidenceAndServiceGaps , fw:Find_IK_WaysFirstReviewDefects , fw:Find_IK_WaysUncheckedPoints ;
    backlog:statesBestPractice "Say in the record what a limit does not cover, and give a way to clear an obstacle only when it makes the obstacle go." ,
        "Review again after every repair: each round found what the last repair left, and the later rounds found faults of the repair itself." .

# Outcome of the objectives of Lineage 29 recorded at its close (see the closure report): Retrospective, the counts read what they read.
fw:Obj_IK_MissionMet backlog:hasAchievementStatus backlog:Ach_Retrospective ; backlog:hasRationale "Counted at the close of Lineage 29 on 2026-11-02: the last observation stands at the target; the checkpoint of 2026-11-03 is not waited for, because the work finished ahead of its base date." .
