# ---- Ruling G197, 2026-11-04: a date of an objective is a forecast, never an enforcement ----
fw:Ruling_G197 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G197" ;
    rdfs:label "A planned date is a forecast and enforces nothing: no work waits for it and no register is invalid because it has passed"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The date of an objective's checkpoint is a forecast of when the work is expected to be done at the pace delivered; it is never a target, a deadline or a promise. Nothing in the framework waits for a date or is enforced by one, because no scheduler exists: work starts and ends when the work allows. A checkpoint date that has passed with no observation is an advisory about the forecast, not a violation, and dates are read afterwards against what happened." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:CheckpointObservedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "LINEAGE_RULING_NARRATIVES v159.0.0, section G197; Owner direction of 2026-11-04 09:17 Istanbul." .
fw:Ruling_G197 backlog:rulingDecides backlog:RS_PlannedDates .

# The rationale of the mission names the outcome it claimed when it closed (Out_Achieved); the mission is in flight again by the reactivation. The link below is the plain reference to that earlier claim (BP-D57).
fw:Mission_ImpedimentsKnown rdfs:seeAlso backlog:Out_Achieved .

