fw:Find_IK_SessionStartNotWord a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_IK_Preflight ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Session start reads the word NOT in the OE ceremony output as a refusal, and the ceremony prints '0 NOT MEASURED' on a clean run, so session start says NOT READY although the ceremony says PROCEED (found on 2026-11-04 when the new OE discipline arrived)." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Open item: narrow the reading to a refusal line; the tool belongs to a closed lineage, so it goes through a change request." .
fw:Find_IK_OverflowCaseUncovered a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_IK_DatesReport ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The fix for a date outside the calendar after conversion to UTC was made after the review and has no case of its own in the dates probe." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Open item for the next change to the probe." .
fw:Find_IK_BumpNamedByReview a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_IK_Preflight ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The review judged the preflight probe's bump should be a minor one (new cases and mutants); it was renamed 1.0.0 to 1.1.0 and the other bumps stand. The OE discipline of 2026-11-04 asks that the impact of each change be stated; the changelog of the release does." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Applied." .
fw:Find_IK_MissionCountDidNotMove a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_IK_DatesReport ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The count of unsatisfied deliverables stayed at 7 after this box, because each of the deliverables these stories serve (enforcement, reports) has another story still open; the objectives of the area moved (4 to 3, 2 to 1)." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Read the area objectives for progress; the mission count moves when a deliverable's last story is done." .
