# ---- Lineage 29, box 6 (G199): kinds of earlier findings, ways that fit, an obstacle that names its box ----
# Findings that carried no kind are given one; three whose recorded kind was wrong are read again (the recorded kind stays).
fw:Find_ChangelogHeaderLoss backlog:hasImpedimentKind backlog:Imp_ToolFault .
fw:Find_SelfReferentialProofPath backlog:hasImpedimentKind backlog:Imp_ToolFault .
fw:Find_SymmetricDivergenceRule backlog:hasImpedimentKind backlog:Imp_ToolFault .

# A way that supplies missing evidence, a way beyond a retry, and the limit of redoing steps
backlog:Mth_MeasureAndRecord a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ClearingMethod ;
    backlog:isFrameworkOriginal true ;
    rdfs:label "Measure what the claim rests on and record it"@en ;
    skos:definition "Where the evidence is missing and can be produced, produce it: run the measurement or the test drive on the smallest case that shows the claim, keep the figure and how it was got in the package, and let the claim say only what that figure shows. Gone when a reader can see the figure and its method in the package and the claim does not go beyond it."@en .
backlog:Imp_EvidenceGap backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_MeasureAndRecord .
backlog:Imp_ServiceFailure backlog:clearableBy backlog:Mth_UseAllowedRoute .
backlog:Mth_RedoInOrder skos:scopeNote "Applies to work not yet released. A released record is appended to and never edited, so a step done early or late in a released file is put right by a new record or a new version, and a bypassed stage is never backfilled (restart the chain)."@en .

# An obstacle names the box whose work it blocks
fw:Imp_IK_1 backlog:impedes fw:It_IK_2 .

# The ruling that decides the box
fw:Ruling_G199 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G199" ;
    rdfs:label "A finding has a kind, a kind has ways that fit it, and an obstacle names the box it blocks"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "Every retrospective finding recorded before Lineage 29 closed names the kind of obstacle that is its root cause (the findings of Lineage 29 and of later lineages are not yet bound); where a later reading finds the recorded kind wrong, the recorded kind stays and the kind it is read as is recorded beside it, because a committed record is appended to and never edited. Every kind of obstacle has a way that fits it: missing evidence can be produced and recorded, a failed outside service has a route beyond the retry, and the ways for work in the wrong order agree that a released record is never edited. An impediment of a lineage that adopts RS_ImpedimentsKnown names the box (iteration) whose work it blocks. It is recorded when it is met, with the time it was raised, and the tool refuses a box of another lineage and a time before the box began; the release of a closed box can still be blocked." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:ImpedimentNamesBoxShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "LINEAGE_RULING_NARRATIVES v161.0.0, section G199; Lineage 29 box 6 of 2026-11-04." .
fw:Ruling_G199 backlog:rulingDecides backlog:RS_ImpedimentsKnown .
