# ---- Ruling G200, 2026-11-04: the scope taxonomy is a tree whose areas and exclusions are answered (the taxonomy link of Lineage 29) ----
backlog:RS_ScopeItemsAnswered a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:RuleSet ;
    rdfs:label "Every area and exclusion of the scope is answered by a goal of its own"@en ;
    skos:definition "Within an adopting lineage whose goals exist, each area of its scope statement has a scope-facing (or containment-facing) goal that covers it and each exclusion has an exclusion-facing goal that guards it, unless it sits under a parent of its own kind. A RuleSet because it binds only lineages that adopt it; a lineage opened earlier is not bound, and the older advisory about the same thing stays as it was."@en .
backlog:Pr_15 a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ProfileRevision ; rdfs:label "Profile revision 15"@en ; backlog:revisionNumber 15 ; skos:definition "Adds to the agentic adaptive profile (AAL) the rule set that every area and exclusion of the scope is answered by a goal, so that a lineage opened under it cannot leave a scope item without someone answerable for it. The other profiles are not changed."@en .
backlog:Profile_AgenticAdaptive backlog:profileIncludes backlog:RS_ScopeItemsAnswered .
backlog:RS_ScopeItemsAnswered backlog:introducedInRevision backlog:Pr_15 .
backlog:RS_PackagesRequired a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:RuleSet ;
    rdfs:label "A roadmap is built from packages (G219)"@en ;
    skos:definition "Within an adopting lineage that has its backlog, the roadmap names at least one package (what is deployed when and with which items); even the simplest lineage has one package, which delivers all its deliverables; every deliverable is delivered by a package; a package traces to a deliverable, so the number of packages is measured from the scope and is never more than its deliverables; and an item an iteration plans belongs to a package that targets that iteration. A RuleSet because it binds only lineages that adopt it; lineages opened earlier are not bound."@en .
backlog:Pr_16 a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ProfileRevision ; rdfs:label "Profile revision 16"@en ; backlog:revisionNumber 16 ; skos:definition "Adds to the agentic adaptive profile (AAL) the rule set that a roadmap is built from packages, so that a lineage opened under it names what is deployed when and plans its sprints to match. The other profiles are not changed."@en .
backlog:Profile_AgenticAdaptive backlog:profileIncludes backlog:RS_PackagesRequired .
backlog:RS_PackagesRequired backlog:introducedInRevision backlog:Pr_16 .
fw:Ruling_G200 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G200" ;
    rdfs:label "Scope items form trees, and every area and exclusion of an adopting lineage is answered by a goal"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "An area, a deliverable, an exclusion or a goal may sit under one parent of its own kind (hasParentItem), so each kind forms a tree; an item with no parent sits under its scope statement or mission. A lineage that adopts RS_ScopeItemsAnswered, once its goals exist, answers each area and each exclusion of its scope with a goal of its own or a parent of its own kind. AAL includes the rule set from profile revision 15; the other profiles and the lineages opened earlier are unchanged. An area that is the product view of another area is exempt. Deliverables are not checked by this rule. A cycle of parents and a second parent are not refused. Every scope statement of the lineage is read, a retracted one included." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:ScopeItemUnansweredShape , backlog:ParentItemShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "LINEAGE_RULING_NARRATIVES v162.0.0, section G200; Owner direction of 2026-11-03 (the missing parent-child link, and every scope item answered by its own goal)." .
fw:Ruling_G200 backlog:rulingDecides backlog:RS_ScopeItemsAnswered , backlog:Pr_15 , backlog:Profile_AgenticAdaptive .

