# ---- Lineage 29, change request of 2026-11-05: what the lineage still owes before it can end honestly ----
# Requested by the Owner on 2026-11-05 at 01:07 Istanbul, after an independent review found that a closure written without these pieces overstated the result. Routed here first (G195): a change request, then scope items, goals, objectives and stories; nothing below is built before its route is recorded.
fw:CR_C29_Completion a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by what it still owes before it can end: each gap traced to its answer, each repair reviewed again, an honest outcome and a reason for every objective"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope2_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "The lineage was closed once as achieved and reopened because the result was overstated. A second closure was written and an independent review found it overstated again: none of the thirteen gaps found after the first closure is linked to the work that answers it; three of them are answered only in part (the late record of an obstacle is still accepted, the kinds given to earlier findings are readings, and the rule that every scope item has a goal binds only lineages opened from now); the repairs that followed refused reviews were never reviewed again; the outcome partly achieved, promised on 2 November, does not exist; and the objectives would all have been closed with one identical reason. Three scope items answer this: a traced answer or a stated disposition for each gap; a second review of every repair made after a refused review; and an outcome of partly achieved with a status and a reason for each objective. The five guard objectives are observed in the closing box and need no new scope. Requested by the Owner on 2026-11-05 (option 1: keep the lineage open and provide a way for proper completion); decided when the chain is rebuilt." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission2 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_Completion a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by what it still owes"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_Completion ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Computed from the register and the review of 2026-11-05: 13 post-closure gaps, of which 3 are answered in part; 47 findings of the lineage cited by no closure; 3 boxes (6, 7, 8) whose repairs after a refused review have one review each; 19 objectives, 5 of them never observed after their starting value. The scope gains three areas and three deliverables; the eight areas, eleven deliverables and five exclusions already held stand, and the eleven satisfied deliverables stay satisfied. The chain is rebuilt from the scope by a third revision, with three stories added (one box each, each checked by a fresh agent); the closure is written after them and confirmed by the Owner. No other lineage is touched. Nothing here changes a rule of any profile; the outcome of partly achieved is a new value of the vocabulary, built by its own story." .

# ---- Ruling G201, 2026-11-05: Lineage 29 stays open until its owed work is done and the Owner confirms the closure ----
fw:Ruling_G201 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G201" ;
    rdfs:label "Lineage 29 stays open until what it owes is done and the Owner confirms its closure"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The mission of Lineage 29 is not recorded as achieved on the lineage's own counts: it stays reopened while a change request grows its scope by what it still owes, and is closed only after those stories are done, each gap traced to its answer, and the Owner confirms a closure report that states its limits. The shape checks that a closure report exists; it does not check the Owner's confirmation, which this ruling records and nothing carries out." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:MissionClosureRequiresReportShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-04 22:07 UTC, which is 2026-11-05 01:07 Istanbul (option 1: keep the lineage open and provide a way for proper completion, through change management); the review of 2026-11-05 that found the second closure overstated." ;
    backlog:rulingDecides fw:CR_C29_Completion .

# ---- Change request, 2026-11-05: safeguards against an overstated closure, and monitoring of the method until they enforce ----
fw:CR_C29_Safeguards a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by ten safeguards that stop a lineage from being closed as achieved while its gaps and repairs are unanswered, and by monitoring of the method until they enforce"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope2_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Lineage 29 was closed as achieved twice and both closures were overstated. An independent analysis of the fifteen reviews of the lineage counted 144 defects and found eight root causes; the deepest is an asymmetry: a failing exit needs an assessment, while an achieved exit needs only text. Ten safeguards answer them: a review verdict recorded by the tool, with Done depending on it; an objective marked retrospective cannot be moved by work; every gap found after a closure is answered by a link before the lineage can be achieved; a repair made after a refused review is reviewed again; every reported measure has a query that computes it; every probe proves it catches a deliberate fault; every rule set has an adopter; a closure marked achieved carries an as-is assessment and the Owner's confirmation; a judged classification is read a second time; and the reviewer's brief is generated from a frozen state. Until they enforce, a report-only monitor measures each of them against its baseline. Each becomes a scope item, then a goal, an objective and a story, in the order of the lineage chain; none is built before its story is planned." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission2 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_Safeguards a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by the ten safeguards and the monitoring of the method"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_Safeguards ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "The scope gains ten deliverables (one per safeguard) and one for the monitoring of the method; the areas, deliverables and exclusions already held stand. The chain is rebuilt from the scope by a stage revision, one release per stage, with one story per safeguard and one for the monitor, each in a box checked by a fresh reviewer. Rules of the lineage discipline that the safeguards bring are added in the release that ships the shapes enforcing them, each under a dated ruling of the Owner. Shapes that tighten a rule are breaking changes for registers that use them and bump the version accordingly. The monitor and the analysis written before this request was recorded are set aside and enter only through their stories. No other lineage is touched; the closure of Lineage 29 waits for these stories as well as for the change request that grows its scope by what it still owes." .

# ---- Ruling G202, 2026-11-05: the safeguards are built as planned work of Lineage 29, never ad hoc ----
fw:Ruling_G202 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G202" ;
    rdfs:label "The ten safeguards against an overstated closure, and the monitoring of the method, are built as planned work of Lineage 29"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The Owner's instruction to find the root causes of the overstated closures, add preventive mechanisms and interim monitoring, and add the enforcements to the lineage discipline serves the mission of Lineage 29 and is routed as a change request of that lineage, building all ten safeguards in one batch. Each safeguard is a story of the lineage chain; the rule it brings into the lineage discipline is added in the release that ships its enforcing shape, under a dated ruling of the Owner. The shapes named here check that the request supports the mission and is assessed before it is decided; that each safeguard is planned before it is built is checked by the release gate, and the content of each safeguard is checked by its own story." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:ChangeSupportsMissionShape , backlog:DispositionRequiresAssessmentShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-05 06:25 UTC, which is 2026-11-05 09:25 Istanbul (option 2: all ten mechanisms at once, continuing in a safe position for the next phases), on his instruction of 2026-11-05 06:07 UTC, which is 09:07 Istanbul (find the root causes first, add preventive mechanisms, add interim measures to monitor the method, and update the lineage discipline with the enforcements); and his approval of 2026-11-05 06:49 UTC, which is 09:49 Istanbul, to redo the routing after the first attempt drifted." ;
    backlog:rulingDecides fw:CR_C29_Safeguards .

# ---- Ruling G203, 2026-11-05: each increment of a lineage is witnessed on a work branch; the main line receives the batch ----
fw:Ruling_G203 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G203" ;
    rdfs:label "Each stage and each box of a lineage is witnessed by its own commit on a work branch, and the main line receives the finished batch in one release"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "A lineage may name a work branch on the governed repository where its increments are witnessed: every stage and every box closes in its own commit on that branch, pushed when it closes, with the checks that fit its kind of work run locally first. The main line receives the batch in one release once the summaries and measures meet the expected conditions; otherwise the work is reworked on the branch. The order check reads the first appearance of the lineage's stages and items on the branch the lineage names, and a recorded commit must be an ancestor of that branch. The branch is never rewritten; changes of the main line are merged into it, not rebased onto it. The shapes named here check that consecutive stages record different commits and that every stage output is complete; the order on the branch is checked by the order check, which no shape can do. Not checked: when each commit was pushed; the order rests on ancestry, as on the main line." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:StageOrderWitnessShape , backlog:StageOutputShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-05 07:45 UTC, which is 10:45 Istanbul (option 1: test the push of a work branch, then build it), on his proposal of 07:42 UTC, which is 10:42 Istanbul (keep the progress in the local environment until ready, run the monitor and control ceremonies of each type of work locally, and at the end collect the summaries, make the measures and decide to commit or rework). The push of a work branch was tested the same minute and works; deleting a branch from this workspace is refused." .

# ---- Change request, 2026-11-05: the stage digests do not cover the link from an objective to the work that can move it (handover of the Agentic Systems package, item 2) ----
fw:CR_C29_MoverDigest a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by a stage digest that sees a change of the work that can move an objective"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope2_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the Agentic Systems package on 2026-11-05 and verified the same day against the digest tool: a stage digest is computed over the names of the records a stage holds, never over their links, so the work named as able to move an objective can be added, removed or replaced with no digest changing. An objective that work can move silently is the root of the overstated closures this lineage answers; the gap belongs to the safeguards against them. The deliverable: the objective stage's digest covers the link from an objective to the work that can move it, or the discipline states why it does not." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission2 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_MoverDigest a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of a stage digest that sees a change of the work that can move an objective"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_MoverDigest ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One deliverable under the closure safeguards. Covering the link in the digest changes the digest of every objective stage already recorded, so a new digest table is needed that only lineages adopting it read; the recorded digests of other lineages stay as they are. No other lineage is touched." .

# ---- Lineage 29 is witnessed on its work branch from the third chain on (G203) ----
fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:witnessedOnBranch "wip/brsf-l29-chain3" .
fw:Ruling_G203 rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (after the independent review of the first version of the mechanism): origin is asked which commit it holds for the branch and the fetched ref must be that commit, so a branch deleted on origin, an unreachable origin and a fetch that fails or does not finish are a broken witness; and, for every lineage, a commit or release that an active stage output records must hold that output (order check 1.18.0). The rule that a lineage which names no branch publishes each increment stands." .

# ---- Post-closure finding, 2026-11-05: the four outputs of the second chain name a release that does not hold them ----
fw:Find_C29_WrongClosedAtCommit a backlog:PostClosureFinding ; rdfs:label "The four stage outputs of the second chain of Lineage 29 name release 4.8.0 as the commit they closed at, and that release holds none of them"@en ;
    backlog:declaresGapFor fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:describesUncoveredScope "The scope, goal, objective and backlog outputs of the second chain of Lineage 29 record release 4.8.0 as the commit they closed at. None of them is in that release: all four first appear together in release 4.9.0. The order of the second chain was therefore never witnessed, and the record said it was. The order check let it through because it asked only whether the recorded release is an ancestor of the tip, never whether it holds the output." ;
    backlog:hasFindingScale backlog:Scale_Systemic ;
    backlog:findingRaisedAt "2026-11-05T09:20:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:findingEvidence fw:Ev_C29_WrongClosedAtCommit .
fw:Ev_C29_WrongClosedAtCommit a backlog:Evidence ; rdfs:label "Evidence for: the four stage outputs of the second chain of Lineage 29 name a release that does not hold them"@en ; backlog:evidenceVerified true ;
    backlog:verifiedByTool "git log -S and git merge-base on the governed repository; the order check 1.18.0" ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "For every active stage output of every live lineage that records a commit or release, its first appearance under the register path was compared with the recorded commit: 55 hold their output, 4 do not, all four of Lineage 29 (recorded release 4.8.0, first appearance a42fb600, which is release 4.9.0). Would the outcome have occurred without the safeguards? Yes: no safeguard compared a recorded commit with the output it closes, so this is a gap, not a safeguard working (L-114)." .
fw:Out_Scope2_ImpedimentsKnown rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (correction): this output does not appear in release 4.8.0, which it records as its commit; it first appears in release 4.9.0 (a42fb600), together with the goal, objective and backlog outputs of the same chain. The record is not rewritten; see the post-closure finding on the release named." .
fw:Out_Goal2_ImpedimentsKnown rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (correction): this output does not appear in release 4.8.0, which it records as its commit; it first appears in release 4.9.0 (a42fb600), together with the scope, objective and backlog outputs of the same chain. The record is not rewritten; see the post-closure finding on the release named." .
fw:Out_Objective2_ImpedimentsKnown rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (correction): this output does not appear in release 4.8.0, which it records as its commit; it first appears in release 4.9.0 (a42fb600), together with the scope, goal and backlog outputs of the same chain. The record is not rewritten; see the post-closure finding on the release named." .
