# ---- Change requests, 2026-11-05: two gaps received after the third chain was planned; each enters the next batch of Lineage 29 through its chain ----
fw:CR_C29_OutcomeLatest a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by an objective outcome read the same way by its definition and its rule"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the OE governance session on 2026-11-05 (P13, P14) and verified the same day: the definition of an objective's outcome reads its latest observation, while the rule that marks it met fires on any observation that reaches the target, so an objective that reached its target once and fell back reads met. An objective read as met when it is not is an overstated closure, which the safeguards of this lineage answer. The deliverable: the rule and the definition read the same observation, and an acceptance criterion asks only for what the register can record." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_OutcomeLatest a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of an objective outcome read the same way by its definition and its rule"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_OutcomeLatest ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One deliverable under the closure safeguards. Changing which observation counts may change the outcome of objectives of other lineages that have fallen back after reaching their target; their outcomes are measured before the change and every difference is listed. Which observation counts is decided with the Owner when the deliverable is planned." .
fw:CR_C29_GrantAuthorization a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by an authorization from the Owner behind every grant of a reviewer's access given by an agent"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the Agentic Systems package on 2026-11-05 (its corrected reply on who may give a verifier's access) and verified the same day: its shapes accept an agent as the giver of access only under a recorded authorization from a person, naming the place as a link, the mode, the period and the place's builder; all 23 grants of this register are given by an agent and none has such an authorization. The grantor of the reviewers' access is an area of this lineage's scope, which the second chain closed on a record the other package now refuses. The deliverable: every grant given by an agent stands on a recorded authorization of the Owner, or the difference between the two packages is stated and decided by the Owner." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_GrantAuthorization a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of an authorization behind every grant of a reviewer's access given by an agent"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_GrantAuthorization ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One deliverable under the accountability area. The 23 existing grants gain an authorization record appended beside them (they are not rewritten), and the box tool records one for each new grant. The vocabulary of the Agentic Systems package is read, not changed." .

