# ---- Ruling G204, 2026-11-05: the work deferred from the handovers enters Lineage 29 as change requests ----
fw:CR_C29_TypedWithdrawal a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by a typed way to withdraw a record that was written wrongly, instead of an appended comment"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the OE governance session on 2026-11-05 and verified the same day: the vocabulary has no withdrawal property; retraction exists only for stage outputs, and supersession only for missions, rules and governed documents. Met again in this lineage the same day: the four outputs of the second chain, and 59 notes after the last review, could be corrected only by an appended comment that a reader must find. A closure that cannot withdraw a wrong record cannot be shown honest. Link to the mission: Direct: the overstated closures of this lineage were left standing for lack of a way to withdraw them." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_TypedWithdrawal a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by a typed way to withdraw a record that was written wrongly, instead of an appended comment"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_TypedWithdrawal ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One deliverable under the closure area. A withdrawal is a new record that points at the one it withdraws; nothing committed is rewritten. Existing corrections stay as comments; the withdrawal is used from now on, and the shapes that read stage outputs learn to skip a withdrawn record." .
fw:CR_C29_EvidenceReader a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by a link from every evidence record to the executor who read it"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the OE governance session on 2026-11-05 and verified the same day: no property of the vocabulary links an evidence record to an executor instance; the tool that verified it is a string. The reviews of this lineage are evidence that an independent agent read the work, and that fact cannot be checked as a link. Link to the mission: Direct: an independent review is the answer to an overstated result, and it must be a link, not text." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_EvidenceReader a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by a link from every evidence record to the executor who read it"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_EvidenceReader ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One deliverable under the accountability area. A new link from evidence to its reader; the existing 23 grants and the reviews gain the link by appended records, none is rewritten. The string stays readable and is marked as the older form." .
fw:CR_C29_RealMeasures a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by objectives that measure the reality a goal wants and a goal read from them, with an approved table for every band"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the OE governance session on 2026-11-05 (ten gaps, P15 to P24, found in another package's lineage that was conformant throughout). It is the failure this lineage was reopened for: objectives that count the work's own output pass every shape; a checkpoint that waits on a work item is accepted in place of a measure; a goal has no score; the range of the success-metric link is nominal and not enforced (verified in the vocabulary). The first objectives of this lineage were rejected for the same reason. Link to the mission: Direct: it is the same overstatement, seen from the objectives." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_RealMeasures a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by objectives that measure the reality a goal wants and a goal read from them, with an approved table for every band"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_RealMeasures ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Eight to ten deliverables, one per gap that the framework can answer (a roll-up of a goal, the difference between a control point and a measure, a metric that names its formula and confidence, a state for a threshold table not yet approved, a check that a measure can fall, a derivation that can be run). Grows the objectives of this lineage: each is re-read against it and the difference is listed. Thresholds are proposed to the Owner, never enforced before he approves them." .
fw:CR_C29_ChangeIntroducedElements a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by a scope change that can name the goals and objectives it introduces, and a stage digest that follows them"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the another registrant package on 2026-11-04 and verified on 2026-11-05: the admission link of a scope change has the work item as its range, so a change cannot name a goal or an objective it introduces. This lineage met it: its third chain re-admitted eleven stories and eleven tasks of the second chain through the output of the backlog stage, as a disclosed workaround. Link to the mission: Direct: the same gap as the digest of work that moves an objective, which this lineage already owes." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_ChangeIntroducedElements a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by a scope change that can name the goals and objectives it introduces, and a stage digest that follows them"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_ChangeIntroducedElements ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One deliverable under the repairs area, planned beside the digest repair already accepted. The range widens to the elements of the chain; the digest of the stage that follows includes them. The eleven re-admissions stay as recorded." .
fw:CR_C29_ScopeTaxonomy a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by traceability from the scope taxonomy: every scope item answered, in the register and not only for lineages opened from now"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the OE governance session and answered by this package as accepted in substance: the rules the OE session asks for match what the shapes allow today and no route was found that already refuses the gaps. They are scope changes of the framework, entering the next lineage cycle. This lineage is the one that found that the rule that every scope item has a goal binds only lineages opened from now. Link to the mission: Direct: a gap answered in part is one of the thirteen gaps of this lineage." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_ScopeTaxonomy a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by traceability from the scope taxonomy: every scope item answered, in the register and not only for lineages opened from now"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_ScopeTaxonomy ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One to three deliverables under the gaps area, from the handover's own list; the list is read in full when the deliverables are written. The shapes bind lineages already open, with the older ones listed as exceptions, not silently passed." .
fw:CR_C29_ValidatorOutcomeState a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by one reading of whether a scope's outcome is derived, whatever the state of the backlog container"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the agentic-sdlc package on 2026-11-04 in two handovers: on the same data the validator 1.19.0 reports a scope whose work is complete as having no derived outcome when the backlog container is Done, and does not when it is InProgress; v1.18.0 reported it in neither. Not reproduced here, the sender's register bytes are not in this package. The sender records the finding as accepted, and its check fails if the finding stops. Link to the mission: Indirect, and stated so: a scope outcome that is derived or not by the state of a container is a different way of reading a result as achieved. The Owner decided it enters." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_ValidatorOutcomeState a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by one reading of whether a scope's outcome is derived, whatever the state of the backlog container"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_ValidatorOutcomeState ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One deliverable under the outcome area. First the finding is reproduced on a planted register in both validator versions, then the right reading is decided and the other is repaired. If it cannot be reproduced, the story records that and ends." .
fw:CR_C29_DatePlanOtherRegisters a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by a date planner that forecasts for the registers of other packages and reads a date-time without a zone"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the OE governance session and the another registrant package: the planner reads the framework's own prefix unconditionally (verified in the tool), and stops on a date-time written without a time zone. Link to the mission: Indirect, and stated so: forecasts are not the result of this lineage. It is included on the Owner's decision; forecasts stay forecasts and enforce nothing." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_DatePlanOtherRegisters a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by a date planner that forecasts for the registers of other packages and reads a date-time without a zone"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_DatePlanOtherRegisters ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One deliverable under the monitor area. The planner takes the register's namespace as an input and reads an unzoned date-time as UTC, with a plain message naming the value when it cannot." .
fw:CR_C29_PaceModel a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by a first forecast of pace and effort for a lineage that has no pace of its own, improved by what the packages report back"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the agentic-sdlc package on 2026-11-04 and verified on 2026-11-05: the planner stops when the register has no pair of consecutive boxes with effort, so every new lineage meets the same wall at its objective stage. The sender asks for a prior by kind of work, with the sources named, a way to hand back observations, and that dates stay forecasts. Link to the mission: Indirect, and stated so: the link to the mission is that a forecast stated as assumed, not observed, is an honest figure. The Owner decided it enters." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_PaceModel a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by a first forecast of pace and effort for a lineage that has no pace of its own, improved by what the packages report back"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_PaceModel ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One deliverable under the monitor area, built after the date planner above. It starts from what the registers and handover logs already hold; zero observed boxes is a legal and honest value; nothing waits for a date." .
fw:CR_C29_BoxToolOtherRegisters a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by a box tool that works on the register of any package, not only the framework's own"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the another registrant package on 2026-11-04 and verified on 2026-11-05: the box tool writes the framework's own prefix literally, so a lineage kept in a package register cannot open a box or record a start with it and had to write its own step script. Link to the mission: Indirect, and stated so: the boxes of this lineage are checked by a recorded review, and a lineage elsewhere that cannot use the tool cannot be held to it. The Owner decided it enters." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_BoxToolOtherRegisters a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by a box tool that works on the register of any package, not only the framework's own"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_BoxToolOtherRegisters ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One deliverable under the repairs area. The tool takes the register's namespace as an input; the framework's own register is the default, so nothing changes for it." .
fw:CR_C29_MissionReplacement a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 by a recorded way to replace the mission of a running lineage without breaking the digests of its stages, or a statement that a new lineage is the way"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Received from the another registrant package on 2026-11-04: the Owner decided to replace a lineage's mission, the scope change fits only growth, and re-pointing the mission broke the digest of its own stage. The only working route was to set the old lineage down and open a new one. Link to the mission: Indirect, and stated so: the mission of this lineage has changed hands in meaning more than once. The Owner decided it enters." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission3 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_MissionReplacement a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of Lineage 29 by a recorded way to replace the mission of a running lineage without breaking the digests of its stages, or a statement that a new lineage is the way"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_MissionReplacement ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "One deliverable under the closure area. The route or the statement goes into the lineage discipline, which stands exactly at its size ceiling, so room is made first; the rule is enforced by a named shape under a dated ruling." .
fw:Ruling_G204 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G204" ;
    rdfs:label "The work deferred from the handovers enters Lineage 29 as change requests, each stating how it supports the mission"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The Owner asked that the work deferred from the handovers be added into the current lineage, because it is very critical. It is routed as change requests of Lineage 29, one for each subject, with an impact assessment each; where the link to the mission is indirect the request says so. Each enters the chain as a scope item first, then a goal, an objective and a story, in small iterations and batch releases. Each request stays pending until its scope change is written, which needs its stories in the chain; accepting one without them would record a decision that left nothing behind. The two change requests of the same day that were pending enter the same way. Nothing is built before it is planned." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:ChangeSupportsMissionShape , backlog:DispositionRequiresAssessmentShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-05 10:55 UTC, which is 13:55 Istanbul (add the deferred work into the current lineage; it is very critical)." ;
    backlog:rulingDecides fw:CR_C29_OutcomeLatest , fw:CR_C29_GrantAuthorization , fw:CR_C29_TypedWithdrawal , fw:CR_C29_EvidenceReader , fw:CR_C29_RealMeasures , fw:CR_C29_ChangeIntroducedElements , fw:CR_C29_ScopeTaxonomy , fw:CR_C29_ValidatorOutcomeState , fw:CR_C29_DatePlanOtherRegisters , fw:CR_C29_PaceModel , fw:CR_C29_BoxToolOtherRegisters , fw:CR_C29_MissionReplacement .
fw:CR_C29_ChangeIntroducedElements rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (a further handover, from the agentic-sdlc package, after this request was written): a lineage that follows the rules moved from a passing to a failing stage digest by adding deliverables, goals and objectives through an accepted change; two readings are offered, leave the added elements out of the digests or let the request record a new digest per stage it touched. The request carries the question; the reading is decided when the deliverable is planned." .

# ---- Lineage 29, fourth stage revision, 2026-11-05: the chain is rebuilt from the Scope stage for the work deferred from the handovers (ruling G204) ----
fw:SRev4_ImpedimentsKnown a backlog:StageRevision ; rdfs:label "Fourth stage revision of Lineage 29: the chain is rebuilt from the Scope stage for the work taken in from the handovers"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The Owner decided on 2026-11-05 10:55 UTC (13:55 Istanbul) that the work deferred from the handovers enters this lineage (G204). Twelve change requests grow the scope: eight new areas and twelve new deliverables, of which two (the outcome read by one observation and the authorization behind a grant) fall under areas the lineage already holds. Every closed stage of the third chain is cumulative, so a new deliverable, goal or objective is a new subject in each stage after the scope and the third chain cannot stand as it is: its four outputs are retracted and the chain is rebuilt, the first three stages deriving their goals, objectives and stories from the third chain where they are kept." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput fw:Out_Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown , fw:Out_Goal3_ImpedimentsKnown , fw:Out_Objective3_ImpedimentsKnown , fw:Out_Backlog3_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
fw:Out_Scope3_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:outputRetracted true .
fw:Out_Goal3_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:outputRetracted true .
fw:Out_Objective3_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:outputRetracted true .
fw:Out_Backlog3_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:outputRetracted true .

# ---- Lineage 29: Scope stage, rebuilt by the fourth revision ----
fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown a backlog:ScopeStatement ; rdfs:label "Scope: the obstacles and the ways to clear them, what the lineage still owes, and the safeguards against an overstated closure"@en ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "Name the obstacles and the ways to clear them and show it in use, and close the lineage only on what is true: the kinds and ways of the first scope are corrected and completed; an obstacle is recorded when it is met and attached to its box; a blocked agent is shown raising, advising on and clearing a real obstacle in a box; the rules about obstacles and about the scope taxonomy are checked; the forecast discussion is recorded and the dates report does not stop; the grantor of the reviewers' access is reconciled; every gap found after the first closure is traced to its answer; every repair made after a review that did not accept is reviewed again; the outcome and every objective carry an honest status with a reason; ten safeguards stop a lineage from being closed as achieved while its gaps and repairs are unanswered, and the stage digests see a change of the work that can move an objective; and the method is monitored until they enforce; the work taken in from the handovers: a record written wrongly can be withdrawn by a link; an evidence record is linked to its reader; objectives measure the reality their goals want; a change can name the goals and objectives it introduces and the closed stages still reproduce; the answering of every scope item by a goal binds lineages already open; a scope outcome is read by one reading; the planning tools work on the register of any package and a lineage with no pace of its own gets a first forecast; the mission of a running lineage can be replaced by a recorded route; an objective outcome is read from one observation; and every grant given by an agent stands on an authorization of the Owner. Nothing else." ;
    backlog:scopeForMission fw:Mission_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ;
    backlog:requiresDeliverable fw:Del_IK_D1 , fw:Del_IK_D2 , fw:Del_IK_D3 , fw:Del_IK_D4 , fw:Del_IK_D5 , fw:Del_IK_D6 , fw:Del_IK_D7 , fw:Del_IK_D8 , fw:Del_IK_D9 , fw:Del_IK_D10 , fw:Del_IK_D11 ,
        fw:Del_IK_D12 , fw:Del_IK_D13 , fw:Del_IK_D14 , fw:Del_IK_D15 , fw:Del_IK_D16 , fw:Del_IK_D17 , fw:Del_IK_D18 , fw:Del_IK_D19 , fw:Del_IK_D20 , fw:Del_IK_D21 , fw:Del_IK_D22 , fw:Del_IK_D23 , fw:Del_IK_D24 , fw:Del_IK_D25 , fw:Del_IK_D26 , fw:Del_IK_D27 , fw:Del_IK_D28 , fw:Del_IK_D29 , fw:Del_IK_D30 , fw:Del_IK_D31 , fw:Del_IK_D32 , fw:Del_IK_D33 , fw:Del_IK_D34 , fw:Del_IK_D35 , fw:Del_IK_D36 , fw:Del_IK_D37 , fw:Del_IK_D38 ;
    backlog:coversArea fw:Area_IK_Kind , fw:Area_IK_Method , fw:Area_IK_Record , fw:Area_IK_Kept , fw:Area_IK_Live , fw:Area_IK_Enforce , fw:Area_IK_Reports , fw:Area_IK_Account ,
        fw:Area_IK_Gaps , fw:Area_IK_Repairs , fw:Area_IK_Outcome , fw:Area_IK_Closure , fw:Area_IK_Monitor , fw:Area_IK_Withdraw , fw:Area_IK_Evidence , fw:Area_IK_Measures , fw:Area_IK_Elements , fw:Area_IK_Taxonomy , fw:Area_IK_Validator , fw:Area_IK_Tools , fw:Area_IK_MissionChange ;
    backlog:hasScopeExclusion fw:Ex_IK_Others , fw:Ex_IK_Packages , fw:Ex_IK_Past , fw:Ex_IK_Risks , fw:Ex_IK_People ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown .
