fw:CR_C29_OutcomeLatest rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (after the independent review of the fourth chain): link to the mission: Direct. An outcome read two ways can close an obstacle as cleared when it is not, which is an overstated closure." .
fw:CR_C29_GrantAuthorization rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (after the independent review of the fourth chain): link to the mission: Indirect. The grant of a reviewer's access without an authorization lets a check be given by a party the Owner did not name, which weakens the evidence behind a closure." .

fw:Ruling_G205 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G205" ;
    rdfs:label "A release of records alone takes the light path however many come in a row"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "A release that changes records alone passes the light gate with no limit on how many come in a row; the full suite and measurement run only when code, data or pages change. This relaxes the second clause of the ruling on the light gate of a chain-stage release, which sent the fifth release of a batch to the full gate" ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:StageOrderWitnessShape , backlog:StageOutputShape ;
    rdfs:seeAlso fw:Ruling_G178 ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-05 12:28 UTC, which is 15:28 Istanbul; enforced by the release tool 1.14.0 (no cap) and its probe 1.3.0." .
fw:CR_C29_ChangeIntroducedElements rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (Owner decision, about 16:40 Istanbul): a closed lineage cannot be changed without a revival. The part of this request that asked the stage digests to follow the goals, objectives and deliverables a change introduces is not built; the revival and the stage revision are the answer, and the repair of the order check for an item admitted again stays." .
fw:ST_IK_Elements rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (Owner decision, about 16:40 Istanbul): not planned. A closed lineage cannot be changed without a revival, so the digests are not made to follow what a change introduces. The story stays proposed as the record of what was asked; it is to be withdrawn when the typed withdrawal of a request exists." .

fw:Ruling_G206 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G206" ;
    rdfs:label "A closed lineage is changed only by a revival, so a closed stage's digest is not made to follow what a change adds"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "A closed lineage cannot be changed without a revival: a change that grows it is made by the revival and a stage revision that rebuilds the chain, and the digest of a closed stage is never made to ignore what a change adds, nor does a change record a new digest for it. No shape can reach this beyond the stage-digest and order checks that already read a revived chain; it is a rule of work" ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:StageOutputShape ;
    rdfs:seeAlso fw:CR_C29_ChangeIntroducedElements ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-05 13:40 UTC, which is 16:40 Istanbul." .
fw:Ruling_G207 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G207" ;
    rdfs:label "The earlier ruling on closed lineages is withdrawn: the question it answered was wrong"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The previous ruling on closed lineages is withdrawn. It answered a question that treated a whole lineage as closed, which the sender's handover implied. The profile lets a closed stage of a running lineage be reopened by change management, so how a closed stage shows what change management adds is still undecided, and nothing is built or ruled on it until the Owner answers the question put correctly. No shape can reach this beyond the checks that already read a rebuilt chain; it is a rule of work" ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:StageOutputShape ;
    rdfs:seeAlso fw:Ruling_G206 ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner correction of 2026-11-05 14:03 UTC, which is 17:03 Istanbul." .
fw:Ruling_G206 dcterms:isReplacedBy fw:Ruling_G207 ;
    rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (Owner correction, 17:03 Istanbul): withdrawn; it answered a wrong question. See the ruling that withdraws it." .
fw:CR_C29_ChangeIntroducedElements rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (Owner correction, 17:03 Istanbul): the note of 16:40 above is withdrawn. The question behind it was wrong; the digest part of this request stays open until the Owner answers the question put correctly." .
fw:ST_IK_Elements rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (Owner correction, 17:03 Istanbul): the note of 16:40 above is withdrawn; the story stays proposed and waits for the Owner's answer." .
fw:Ruling_G208 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G208" ;
    rdfs:label "A closed stage leaves out of its check only what a change names, and an added goal's impact on other goals is analysed and answered"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "When change management adds a goal, an objective or a deliverable to a running lineage after the stage that holds it is closed, the closed stage's digest leaves out only the items an accepted scope change names as introduced by it, so nothing is rebuilt and nothing unnamed can hide. If the added goal affects other goals, an impact analysis that names them and the additional work it calls for are done in the same change. The shapes that enforce this are built by the story of this lineage that carries it, and until they exist this is a rule of work" ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:StageOutputShape ;
    rdfs:seeAlso fw:Ruling_G207 , fw:CR_C29_ChangeIntroducedElements ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-05, recorded at 15:05 UTC, which is 18:05 Istanbul." .
fw:CR_C29_ChangeIntroducedElements rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (Owner decision, recorded 18:05 Istanbul): decided: the closed stages leave out only the items a change names, and an added goal's impact on others is analysed and answered. The digest part of this request is planned work again, carried by its story." .
fw:ST_IK_Elements rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (Owner decision, recorded 18:05 Istanbul): planned. Its criterion also owes the impact analysis of an added goal on the other goals and the work that follows from it." .
fw:Ruling_G208 backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:IntroducedGoalImpactNamedShape , backlog:IntroducedGoalImpactAnsweredShape .
fw:Ruling_G208 rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (release 5.4.0): the two shapes named here enforce the second part of this ruling, the impact analysis of an added goal; the first part, that a closed stage's digest leaves out what an accepted scope change names, is enforced by the pipeline verifier 1.15.0 and its probe, which no shape can reach." .
fw:AC_IK_Elements_Impact a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a scope change that introduces a goal, When the impact analysis of its request names no affected goal and does not say none is affected, or names one and no work that answers it, Then the register is refused." .
fw:ST_IK_Elements backlog:hasAcceptanceCriterion fw:AC_IK_Elements_Impact .
fw:ST_IK_Elements rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-05 (release 5.4.0): built in part and not closed. Built: a scope change names the goals, objectives and deliverables it introduces; under digest table v5 every stage digest that holds them (the cumulative Backlog digest too) leaves out those an accepted change of the same lineage names; the impact analysis of an added goal is checked by two shapes (the analysis names the goals affected or says none, and at least one work item that answers; it is not tied item by item to each affected goal). Not done: the independent review; the count of this story's objective (items re-admitted by an output that no scope change names) is not moved yet: a scope change is decided by the Owner and names what it admits, so naming the 22 needs his decision. A test on a copy that named all 37 admitted items showed nothing about it (26 are already named and 11 are tasks, which the digest table leaves out), so it is not offered as evidence." .

fw:Ruling_G209 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G209" ;
    rdfs:label "The build of the story that carries Ruling G208 is authorised"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The first slice of the story of this lineage that carries Ruling G208 (a scope change names what it introduces, the stage digests follow it, and the impact analysis of an added goal is checked by shapes) is authorised as work of release 5.4.0. The story stays proposed until a box moves it; the work is recorded here, not as a move of the story" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso fw:Ruling_G208 , fw:ST_IK_Elements ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-05, recorded at 17:20 UTC, which is 20:20 Istanbul." .
fw:Ruling_G209 backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape .
fw:Ruling_G210 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G210" ;
    rdfs:label "A request the Owner decided through a scope change is recorded as accepted"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The change request that grew the scope of Lineage 29 by the verified gaps was decided by the Owner on 2026-11-04, and the scope change that fulfils it records the decision; its disposition, left pending, is recorded as accepted. The eleven stories that scope change admits are named by an accepted change. The eleven build tasks carried over by the third Backlog output are not items a scope change names, and the Backlog digest does not hold them" ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:AcceptedRequestNeedsScopeChangeShape ;
    rdfs:seeAlso fw:Ruling_G208 , fw:SC_C29_ScopeGrows ;
    backlog:rulingDecides fw:CR_C29_ScopeGrows ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-05, recorded at 21:15 UTC, which is 2026-11-06 00:15 Istanbul (option 1: record the pending request as accepted and recount)." .
fw:CR_C29_ScopeGrows rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-06 (release 5.4.1, Owner decision recorded 00:15 Istanbul): the disposition, pending since the request was written, is recorded as accepted. The only record changed is this status; the Owner's decision of 2026-11-04 is the one the scope change of this request states." .
fw:Obs_IK_Elements4_Recount a backlog:MetricObservation ; rdfs:label "Recount (fourth chain): items re-admitted to a stage by its output with no accepted change naming them"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_IK_Elements ; backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_IK_Elements4 ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 11.0 ; backlog:observedAt "2026-11-05T21:16:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Recounted 2026-11-06 from the register: of the 22 records, the 11 stories are named by the scope change of the request recorded as accepted in this release; the 11 build tasks are named by none, since a scope change names stories, goals, objectives and deliverables, and the Backlog digest holds no execution task. The baseline of 22 stands as recorded; what the 11 tasks need (a decision of the Owner on the target) is not decided." .
fw:Obj_IK_Elements4 rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-06 (release 5.4.1): the count of 22 included 11 stories that an Owner-decided scope change names (its request is now recorded as accepted); 11 build tasks remain, which no scope change can name. The target of 0 is therefore not reachable by naming; it needs the Owner's decision." .
fw:ST_IK_Elements rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-06 (release 5.4.1): the 22 re-admitted items were checked against the register: 11 stories are named by the scope change of the request now recorded as accepted, and 11 tasks are not scope-change items. No new scope change is made." .
fw:Ruling_G211 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G211" ;
    rdfs:label "An obstacle is any condition that makes progress impossible or puts success at risk, told apart as a problem or a risk"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "An obstacle of the work is not only a blocker: it is any condition present in the work that makes progress impossible, slows it, or puts its success at risk. Each is identified, categorized and mitigated or cleared. It is told apart as a problem when it has happened (an obstacle) and as a risk when it is a probability. The goals of the lineage state what this gives a blocked agent and the register, and their objectives measure those goals. Hypothetical events with no present condition behind them stay with the risk domain. The wording of the mission, the definition of an obstacle, the kinds, the ways and the exclusion of risks that have not occurred are widened by change management in the running lineage, never by a revival" ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:ImpedimentKindShape ;
    rdfs:seeAlso fw:Ruling_G189 , fw:Ruling_G190 , fw:Mission_ImpedimentsKnown , fw:Ex_IK_Risks ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-05, recorded at 22:10 UTC, which is 2026-11-06 01:10 Istanbul (option 1 of the question on the wider reading, with the two categories problem and risk)." .
fw:CR_C29_ObstacleBenefit a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 so that an obstacle is any condition that makes progress impossible or risks success, told apart as a problem or a risk, with the benefit of managing them stated as goals"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Requested by the Owner on 2026-11-06 01:05 Istanbul and decided in principle at 01:10 (ruling G211). The seven kinds, the ways to clear, the definition of an impediment and the mission wording cover what stops or slows work; none covers a condition that only puts success at risk, and no kind says whether a condition is a problem or a risk. The existing goals state conditions of the record, not what obstacle management gives a blocked agent and the register; the mission itself names two benefits: a blocked agent knows what to do next, and the register can say why work ran late. Each becomes a scope item, a goal and an objective before it is a story." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission4 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_C29_ObstacleBenefit a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of widening an obstacle to problems and risks, with benefit goals"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_ObstacleBenefit ;
    backlog:affectsGoal fw:Goal_IK_Kind4 , fw:Goal_IK_Method4 , fw:Goal_IK_Live4 , fw:Goal_IK_Guard_Risks4 , fw:Goal_IK_Mission4 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Computed from the register on 2026-11-06. The mission wording and the definition of an impediment say stops or slows; the seven kinds are all of that sort; two obstacles are recorded live, both refusals by a rule, so the benefit goals start with little data. Affected: the goal of the kinds (kinds for risks to success and the category of problem or risk), the goal of the ways (ways that mitigate, beside those that clear), the goal of the live proof (a risk is shown identified and mitigated, not only a blocker cleared), the guard against recording risks that have not occurred (its exclusion is narrowed by ruling G211 to hypothetical events with no present condition behind them), and the mission goal (its wording). Work called for, to be stories once the goals and objectives are decided: the definition and the category, the kinds for risks, the ways that mitigate, the reading of earlier findings as problems or risks, and the benefit goals with their objectives. Nothing recorded earlier is rewritten." .
fw:CR_C29_ObstacleBenefit rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-06 (release 5.4.2): decided in principle by the Owner (ruling G211) and pending only until the scope change that names its goals, objectives and deliverables is recorded; the goals and objectives are proposed to the Owner first because their measures and targets are chosen, not derived." .

fw:Ruling_G211 backlog:rulingDecides fw:CR_C29_ObstacleBenefit .
fw:IA_C29_ObstacleBenefit rdfs:seeAlso fw:Ruling_G211 .

# ---- 5.4.3: the methods that deal with problems and risks are routed (Owner ruling G212) ----
fw:Ruling_G212 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G212" ;
    rdfs:label "A goal is satisfiable before the lineage closes; a later benefit is tracked, not a goal; a method is proven by a test drive, a toy example or a field standard"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "A goal of a lineage states what the work gives and is satisfiable before the lineage closes, because a goal that can only be met later keeps the lineage open and blocks what comes after it. A benefit that appears after closure is recorded as a benefit, owned and not realised until verified evidence shows it, and is never a goal. A method is shown to work by a test drive, a toy example or conformance to a standard of the field. The treatments of a risk are proven by a test drive on a toy example and a check against the treatment options of ISO 31000. The review of this is a review point; no shape can read whether a goal is reachable before closure." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    rdfs:seeAlso fw:Ruling_G211 , fw:CR_C29_ObstacleBenefit ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decisions of 2026-11-05, recorded at 22:44 UTC and 23:51 UTC, which are 01:44 and 02:51 Istanbul on 2026-11-06." .
fw:Ruling_G212 backlog:rulingDecides fw:CR_C29_ObstacleBenefit .
fw:CR_C29_ObstacleBenefit rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-06 (release 5.4.3): the scope change SC_C29_ObstacleMethods fulfils this request, and the request is recorded accepted. Ruling G212 decides the form of its goals." .

fw:Metric_IK_Know5 a core:Metric ; rdfs:label "Conditions of the toy test drive that the tools cannot record"@en ; skos:definition "Counted in units of: condition."@en .
fw:Metric_IK_Treat5 a core:Metric ; rdfs:label "Treatments of a risk with a way proven by a test drive"@en ; skos:definition "Counted in units of: treatment."@en .
fw:Metric_IK_Prove5 a core:Metric ; rdfs:label "Kinds of problem with a way proven by a recorded test drive"@en ; skos:definition "Counted in units of: kind."@en .

fw:Goal_IK_Know5 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "A blocked agent, or one who sees success at risk, can say at once whether the condition is a problem or a risk and which kind it is, so the next step is known"@en ;
    backlog:contributesToMission fw:Mission_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:derivesFromScope fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea fw:Area_IK_Kind ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ; backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Goal4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
fw:Goal_IK_Treat5 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Whatever the condition, the agent is given a known way that deals with it: clearing for a problem; avoiding, reducing, sharing or accepting for a risk"@en ;
    backlog:contributesToMission fw:Mission_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:derivesFromScope fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea fw:Area_IK_Method ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ; backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Goal4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
fw:Goal_IK_Prove5 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Each of those methods is shown to work on a toy example, and the treatments of a risk to match the field standard, before the lineage closes"@en ;
    backlog:contributesToMission fw:Mission_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:derivesFromScope fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea fw:Area_IK_Live ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ; backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Goal4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .

fw:Obj_IK_Know5 a backlog:Objective ; backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ;
    rdfs:label "Objective (fifth chain): Conditions of the toy test drive that the tools cannot record"@en ;
    backlog:contributesToGoal fw:Goal_IK_Know5 ; backlog:fillsScope fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasSuccessMetric fw:Metric_IK_Know5 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue "1"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Decrease ; backlog:hasCheckpoint fw:CP_IK_Know5 ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Measured on 2026-11-05 by a test drive on a copy of the register: of the toy conditions run (a problem of a known kind, a problem cleared by a way that does not fit its kind, a risk) the tools recorded the first, refused the second as designed, and could not record the risk, so one condition cannot be recorded. The target of zero follows: every toy condition that is a problem or a risk can be recorded under its category." ;
    backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Objective4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown .
fw:CP_IK_Know5 a backlog:ObjectiveCheckpoint ; backlog:checkpointDate "2026-11-07T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .
fw:Obs_IK_Know5 a backlog:MetricObservation ; rdfs:label "Baseline (fifth chain): Conditions of the toy test drive that the tools cannot record"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_IK_Know5 ; backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_IK_Know5 ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 1.0 ; backlog:observedAt "2026-11-05T22:46:04Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Test drive on a copy of the register with the impediment tool: raise and clear of a toy problem passed; the toy risk was refused with the message that its kind is not one of the seven." .

fw:Obj_IK_Treat5 a backlog:Objective ; backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ;
    rdfs:label "Objective (fifth chain): Treatments of a risk with a way proven by a test drive"@en ;
    backlog:contributesToGoal fw:Goal_IK_Treat5 ; backlog:fillsScope fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasSuccessMetric fw:Metric_IK_Treat5 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue "0"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetValue "4"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase ; backlog:hasCheckpoint fw:CP_IK_Treat5 ;
    backlog:hasRationale "The target of four is the number of treatment options of a risk in the field standard ISO 31000 (avoid, reduce, share, accept) as read from a published summary of it on 2026-11-06; the standard itself was not read, so the list is checked against the standard text in the story of the proof." ;
    backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Objective4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown .
fw:CP_IK_Treat5 a backlog:ObjectiveCheckpoint ; backlog:checkpointDate "2026-11-07T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .
fw:Obs_IK_Treat5 a backlog:MetricObservation ; rdfs:label "Baseline (fifth chain): Treatments of a risk with a way proven by a test drive"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_IK_Treat5 ; backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_IK_Treat5 ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 0.0 ; backlog:observedAt "2026-11-05T22:46:04Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Counted from the same test drive: the tool lists ways that clear a problem and none that treats a risk." .

fw:Obj_IK_Prove5 a backlog:Objective ; backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ;
    rdfs:label "Objective (fifth chain): Kinds of problem with a way proven by a recorded test drive"@en ;
    backlog:contributesToGoal fw:Goal_IK_Prove5 ; backlog:fillsScope fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasSuccessMetric fw:Metric_IK_Prove5 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue "0"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetValue "7"^^xsd:decimal ;
    backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase ; backlog:hasCheckpoint fw:CP_IK_Prove5 ;
    backlog:hasRationale "The target of seven is the number of kinds of problem the register holds. The test drive of 2026-11-05 covered one kind end to end (evidence missing, cleared by stating the limit) and the refusal of a way that does not fit another (tool at fault); it was run on a copy and kept in no record, so the baseline is zero recorded." ;
    backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Objective4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown .
fw:CP_IK_Prove5 a backlog:ObjectiveCheckpoint ; backlog:checkpointDate "2026-11-07T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .
fw:Obs_IK_Prove5 a backlog:MetricObservation ; rdfs:label "Baseline (fifth chain): Kinds of problem with a way proven by a recorded test drive"@en ;
    backlog:observesMetric fw:Metric_IK_Prove5 ; backlog:observationFor fw:Obj_IK_Prove5 ;
    backlog:hasObservedValue 0.0 ; backlog:observedAt "2026-11-05T22:46:04Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasObservationMethod "Counted from the register: no record of a test drive for any kind of problem." .

fw:Stakeholder_IK_Owner a core:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "The Owner of the package"@en .
fw:Ben_IK_NextStep a backlog:Benefit ; rdfs:label "A blocked agent knows what to do next"@en ;
    backlog:benefitFor fw:Obj_IK_Prove5 ; backlog:hasBenefitOwner fw:Stakeholder_IK_Owner ;
    backlog:hasBenefitStatement "An agent that meets a problem or sees a risk is told the known ways that fit it and no longer waits for a person to say what to do; observed as the hours an obstacle stays open, read from the register after the lineage closes." ;
    backlog:benefitRealized false .
fw:Ben_IK_WhyLate a backlog:Benefit ; rdfs:label "The register can say why work ran late"@en ;
    backlog:benefitFor fw:Obj_IK_Know5 ; backlog:hasBenefitOwner fw:Stakeholder_IK_Owner ;
    backlog:hasBenefitStatement "A late box can be traced to a recorded problem or a recorded risk that came true; observed as the number of late boxes with no recorded cause, read from the date report after the lineage closes." ;
    backlog:benefitRealized false .
fw:Ben_IK_SeenEarly a backlog:Benefit ; rdfs:label "A threat to success is seen and treated before it stops work"@en ;
    backlog:benefitFor fw:Obj_IK_Treat5 ; backlog:hasBenefitOwner fw:Stakeholder_IK_Owner ;
    backlog:hasBenefitStatement "A risk is recorded with its likelihood and consequence and given a treatment before it becomes a problem; observed as the share of problems that were first recorded as a risk, read from the register after the lineage closes." ;
    backlog:benefitRealized false .
fw:Goal_IK_Know5 backlog:expectsBenefit fw:Ben_IK_WhyLate .
fw:Goal_IK_Treat5 backlog:expectsBenefit fw:Ben_IK_SeenEarly .
fw:Goal_IK_Prove5 backlog:expectsBenefit fw:Ben_IK_NextStep .

fw:Del_IK_D39 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "39.1 A condition is recorded as a problem (it has happened) or a risk (a probability that matters to an objective), a risk carries its likelihood and its consequence, and a shape refuses a risk that lacks either"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_IK_Kind ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "An obstacle has a kind from a known set" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown .
fw:Del_IK_D40 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "40.1 A risk has four known treatments (avoid, reduce, share, accept), each with its steps and what shows it done, offered by the tool beside the ways that clear a problem, and none waives, skips or defers a rule"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_IK_Method ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "An obstacle can be cleared by a known way" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown .
fw:Del_IK_D41 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "41.1 A test drive on a toy example is kept in the package for each of the seven kinds of problem and each of the four treatments of a risk, with a table that sets the treatments against the standard ISO 31000 and says where they differ"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_IK_Live ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "An obstacle can be cleared by a known way" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown .
fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:requiresDeliverable fw:Del_IK_D39 , fw:Del_IK_D40 , fw:Del_IK_D41 .

fw:AC_IK_RiskKind a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a condition that has not happened but could stop work or lower the chance of success, When it is recorded, Then it is a risk with a likelihood and a consequence, a condition that has happened is a problem of one of the seven kinds, and a risk without either value is refused." .
fw:AC_IK_RiskTreat a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given a recorded risk, When the agent asks for the known ways, Then the four treatments are offered with their steps and what shows each done, a treatment is recorded with the risk, and a way that waives, skips or defers a rule is not among them." .
fw:AC_IK_MethodDrive a backlog:AcceptanceCriterion ;
    backlog:hasGherkinText "Given the seven kinds of problem and the four treatments of a risk, When each is run on a toy example, Then every run is kept in the package with its result, and the table against ISO 31000 names each point where a treatment differs from the standard." .

