# ---- 5.4.4: a goal is a requirement met within the development; survey and taxonomy routed (Owner rulings G213, G214) ----
fw:Ruling_G213 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G213" ;
    rdfs:label "A goal belongs to the development and is proven within it; a level reached in operation is a benefit, tracked and never a goal"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "A goal of a lineage is a requirement of the development and is shown satisfied within it, by development or test evidence. The requirements set to reach a level in an operating or business environment can be met and shown; the level itself (benefit, enhancement, prevented risk, solved problem, optimisation, a rise or fall of production, market share, cost, income, profit or volume) can only be measured in operation, sometimes by work outside the systems, and is recorded as a benefit with an owner and verified evidence, tracked after deployment. A goal that waits for an operating environment would hold the lineage open with no way to show success or failure at its end. Qualities wanted of the development itself (ontology-native, OEE compliance, another registrant, blockchain orientation, knowledge bases, databases, LLM, agentic, user experience, usability, architecture) may be goals. The reading of a goal as a requirement or a level is a review point until the shape of the story IK-S54 is built." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape , backlog:BenefitShape ;
    rdfs:seeAlso fw:Ruling_G212 , fw:Ruling_G211 ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-06 at 09:30 Istanbul (06:30 UTC)." .
fw:Ruling_G214 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G214" ;
    rdfs:label "The survey of obstacles is run with another registrant, and an obstacle taxonomy built from it is part of the framework from now on"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "No survey of obstacles is recorded in the package, so one is run now as stage one of another registrant. A goal of this lineage is to build, from that survey, a taxonomy of obstacles with their known types and strategies, and the framework uses it from then on. The goals of the lineage are to be defined taxonomically." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-06 at 09:30 Istanbul (06:30 UTC)." .

fw:CR_C29_ObstacleSurvey a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 with a verified survey of obstacles, a taxonomy built from it, and the telling apart of a goal from a benefit"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Requested by the Owner on 2026-11-06 at 09:30 Istanbul. The goals recorded in 5.4.3 are requirements of the development and stand. Three things are missing: a survey of the field that grounds the kinds and strategies (none is recorded), a taxonomy of obstacles built from it as part of the framework, and a shape that tells a goal from a benefit so that no lineage is held open by a level measurable only in operation." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission4 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:Ruling_G213 backlog:rulingDecides fw:CR_C29_ObstacleSurvey .
fw:Ruling_G214 backlog:rulingDecides fw:CR_C29_ObstacleSurvey .
fw:IA_C29_ObstacleSurvey a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of adding a survey, a taxonomy and the telling apart of a goal from a benefit"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_ObstacleSurvey ;
    backlog:affectsGoal fw:Goal_IK_Kind4 , fw:Goal_IK_Method4 , fw:Goal_IK_Live4 , fw:Goal_IK_Know5 , fw:Goal_IK_Treat5 , fw:Goal_IK_Prove5 ;
    backlog:callsForItem fw:ST_IK_Survey5 , fw:ST_IK_Taxon5 , fw:ST_IK_Split5 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Computed from the register on 2026-11-06. The kinds, the ways and the proof of the lineage all rest on a list of seven kinds that no source supports; the survey tests it and the taxonomy places the kinds, so the goals of the kinds, the ways, the live proof and the three goals of 5.4.3 are affected. The goals of 5.4.3 are requirements proven within the development and stay unchanged. The telling apart of a goal from a benefit adds a shape and changes no recorded goal." .

