# ---- 5.4.5: a finished lineage is concluded and set down; governance work has its own category (Owner ruling G215) ----
backlog:Cat_LineageGovernance a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:InvestmentCategory ; rdfs:label "Lineage governance"@en .
fw:Ruling_G215 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G215" ;
    rdfs:label "A finished lineage is concluded and set down; the work that governs lineages is a category of this lineage until the Delivery lineage and its governing lineage are designed"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "A lineage whose items are all Done or Cancelled and whose objectives meet their targets on their last reading is finished, and a finished lineage is concluded: its closure report states what it measured, learned and could not show, every guard it promised to hold is read again at the end, the Owner confirms the report, the mission is set Achieved or Abandoned, and the lineage is then set down into the archive in the next release. Setting a lineage down never removes what a live lineage uses. Until the comprehensive design of lineage governance, the work that governs lineages (concluding, setting down, pausing, switching, starting, and keeping the lineage metadata) is recorded in this lineage as a category of its own, Lineage governance, so that it can be counted apart from the work of delivery. The lineage whose product work is delivered is named the Delivery lineage; the name of the governing lineage is not yet chosen. The enforcement is advisory first: it is a stipulation proposed to the Owner and is not enforced against real work until the Owner rules on it." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decisions of 2026-11-06 at 11:01 and 11:24 Istanbul (08:01 and 08:24 UTC)." .
fw:CR_C29_Governance a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of Lineage 29 with the concluding and setting down of finished lineages, as governance work"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Requested by the Owner on 2026-11-06 at 11:01 and 11:24 Istanbul. Finished lineages that stay open cost every run of the gate, and a tool that breaks the checks of live lineages when it sets one down is an obstacle that slows every lineage; naming, recording and clearing such obstacles is the mission of this lineage. Measured on 2026-11-06: ten finished lineages are not set down, and setting down the seven that can be archived breaks 63 checks of live lineages on a copy." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission4 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:Ruling_G215 backlog:rulingDecides fw:CR_C29_Governance .
fw:IA_C29_Governance a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of adding the concluding and setting down of finished lineages"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_C29_Governance ;
    backlog:affectsGoal fw:Goal_IK_Live4 ;
    backlog:callsForItem fw:ST_IK_GvKeep6 , fw:ST_IK_GvClose6 , fw:ST_IK_GvRule6 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Computed from the register on 2026-11-06. The goal of the live proof is affected: the lineage that proves the method is itself one of the finished lineages the register must conclude, and the setting down of older lineages changes which records the live proof reads. The three added goals leave every recorded goal unchanged." .

fw:Metric_IK_GvKeep6 a core:Metric ; rdfs:label "Checks of live lineages that fail after the seven archivable lineages are set down"@en ; skos:definition "Counted in units of: check."@en .
