# ---- Owner ruling of 2026-11-07 (G216, G217): the impediments lineage becomes the Governance lineage; its mission is widened by an amendment ----
fw:Ruling_G216 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G216" ;
    rdfs:label "A running lineage's mission is widened only by the Owner's mission amendment, which keeps its wording and says more"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "A stage revision never starts at the mission, and a restart answers a bypass, so a running lineage's mission had no way to be widened. The Owner decides a mission amendment: a record that names one mission, states its new wording, gives the reason and cites the Owner's dated ruling. The new wording contains the mission's wording unchanged and says more, so that everything done under the mission still counts toward it; a mission is never narrowed or replaced. The mission record is not rewritten (corrections are appended); the mission in force is the wording of its latest amendment, and an amendment keeps the wording of every earlier amendment. The enforcement is a stipulation proposed to the Owner and is not enforced against real work until the Owner rules on it." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:MissionAmendmentShape , backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decision of 2026-11-07 at 12:05 Istanbul (09:05 UTC), choosing option 1 of the options set before him: add a narrow mission amendment ('1 is fine I think. Proceed with 1 now')." .
fw:Ruling_G217 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G217" ;
    rdfs:label "The lineage that governs lineages is the Governance lineage; the impediments lineage is it, and the governance taxonomy has thirteen branches"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The lineage that governs the lives of lineages is named the Governance lineage, and the lineage whose product work is delivered the Delivery lineage. Lineage 29, which governs obstacles, becomes the Governance lineage: dealing with impediments is one branch of governance, and its work and stories continue. The governance taxonomy has thirteen branches: direction and mandate; accountability and roles; planning and forecasting; change control; obstacles and urgency; risk; assurance and truthful records; operating cadence; cost and speed of the run; obligations and compliance; benefits; closure, archive and lessons; lineage lifecycle (starting, taking a queued lineage into work, pausing); lineage metadata. It is drawn from the field standards (ISO 38500, ISO 37000, ISO 21502, PMBOK 8, PRINCE2 7, COBIT 2019, Scrum) and from the work of the 28 lineages of the register, where about 85 percent of the stories govern how lineages are run and 15 percent deliver the framework itself. The taxonomy is declared whole, but the lineage is scoped to the smallest closeable slice: the branches with open work (obstacles, lineage lifecycle, lineage metadata); the other branches enter by change management when taken up. Procurement, social responsibility, human behaviour and stakeholder engagement are out: the lineages are run by agents and have one stakeholder, the Owner." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decisions of 2026-11-07: 02:41 (survey the governance branches and sort the history), 03:18 (option 1: declare the taxonomy, scope the lineage to the open branches) and 12:05 (the amendment), Istanbul time; the name Governance lineage on 2026-11-06 at 20:35." .
fw:Ruling_G218 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G218" ;
    rdfs:label "The seed of an urgent pause may be recorded before its own lineage has built its chain; a roadmap needs its packages and the simplest lineage has one"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "An emergency pause cannot be declared without naming the urgent work it covers, and the framework refuses work that appears before its lineage has built its chain. The Owner rules that the single seed item a pause names for another lineage is recorded together with the pause, before that lineage builds its chain; it is read against the pause and not against the chain, and any item that appeared earlier, or that no pause names, or that the pause of its own lineage names, is still a bypass. The Owner also rules that a package is a planning subject and not only a deployment one: a roadmap that names no package is not a roadmap, even the simplest lineage has at least one package, and the number of packages is measured from the scope, the goals, the objectives and the backlog and not declared by hand. The seed rule is enforced from this release by the order check; the package rules are proposals until the urgent lineage that builds them has published its shapes." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decisions of 2026-11-07 at 14:13 (the 2SISA finding is genuine and urgent), 14:33 (the simplest lineage has one package; packages are measured from the chain) and 15:23 (the seed may be recorded with the pause), Istanbul time." .
fw:Ruling_G219 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G219" ;
    rdfs:label "A roadmap is built from packages: the rule set RS_PackagesRequired binds the lineages that adopt it"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The Owner's package rules, recorded as proposals in G218, are enforced for every lineage that adopts the rule set RS_PackagesRequired (profile revision 16, adopted at opening by the agentic adaptive profile): a roadmap names at least one package; a lineage that has its backlog has at least one package, and when it has exactly one that package delivers all its deliverables (the simplest form); every deliverable is delivered by a package; a package delivers a deliverable of the scope, and the number of packages is measured from the scope, the goals, the objectives and the backlog by the package-count tool (deliverables that serve the same goals, leaving out the mission goal, travel together); and an item an iteration plans belongs to a package that targets that iteration. Lineages opened earlier are not bound." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner decisions of 2026-11-07 at 14:33 (the simplest lineage has one package; packages are measured from scope, goals, objectives and backlog), 15:23 (option A with the additions) and 17:36 (the decision is given; adapt the package workflow for the lineage), Istanbul time." .
fw:MA_ImpedimentsKnown a backlog:MissionAmendment ;
    rdfs:label "Mission amendment 1 of the Governance lineage: the lives of lineages are governed, with obstacles one branch of it"@en ;
    backlog:amendsMission fw:Mission_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:amendedMissionStatement "An obstacle that stops or slows the work of a lineage can be named, recorded and cleared: it has a kind from a known set, each kind has the resolution methods known for it, it is recorded when it is met with the work it blocks, and its clearing records the method used, so that a blocked agent knows what to do next and the register can say why work ran late. Beside it, the lives of lineages are governed by known steps and checks that an agent follows without asking: how a lineage starts and is taken into work, how it is paused for an urgent interruption, how it is concluded and set down, and the facts kept about it." ;
    backlog:amendmentReason "The mission named only obstacles, but the Owner holds that dealing with impediments is a job of governance and wants the one lineage to govern the lives of lineages. The rules gave no way to widen a mission (a stage revision cannot start at the mission), so the Owner decided a narrow amendment that keeps the mission's wording and adds to it. Measured on 2026-11-07: the lineage has 50 stories, 17 done and 33 open, all maintenance of how lineages are run and closed." ;
    backlog:amendmentRuling fw:Ruling_G216 , fw:Ruling_G217 ;
    backlog:amendedBy backlog:Owner .
fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown rdfs:label "Governance lineage (Lineage 29): the lives of lineages are governed; obstacles are one branch"@en .
fw:Ruling_G215 rdfs:comment "Appended 2026-11-07 (correction): the name of the governing lineage, left open here, was chosen by the Owner: Governance lineage (see the linked ruling). The ruling is not rewritten." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso fw:Ruling_G217 .

