# ---- Conclusion of Lineage 32 (G215): objectives, closure report. The mission outcome and lineage status wait for the Owner's confirmation. ----
fw:ClosureReport_RNP a backlog:ClosureReport ;
    backlog:closesForMission fw:Mission_RoadmapNeedsPackages ;
    backlog:reportGeneratedAt "2026-11-07T21:40:54Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasClosureSummary "The mission asked that a roadmap be built from packages: it names what is deployed when and with which items, and sprints are planned to match. Urgent, from the finding of the 2SISA project that a roadmap naming no package validated clean. Release 5.5.1 let the urgent lineage start (its seed item). Release 5.5.2 made lineages that adopt the rule set RS_PackagesRequired name packages in the roadmap, have one package at least (exactly one for the simplest form, delivering everything), deliver every deliverable by a package, trace each package to a deliverable, and plan iteration items into a package that targets the iteration; a count tool measures the number of packages from scope, goals, objectives and backlog. Release 5.5.3, from the Owner's instruction of 2026-11-07 at 19:57 Istanbul, made the packages hold the whole backlog: each live item in exactly one package, chosen by recorded priority score, impact and deliverable, never leaning on a later package, Done only when its items and sprints are Done, and a sprint plans one package. Two boxes, each checked by a fresh reviewer who found defects that were repaired. Limits: only lineages opened after the rule set bound by it (this lineage and the earlier ones are not); no live lineage has yet been shown to adopt it and build a roadmap, only test cases and a toy example; technical requirements are carried by dependencies alone; a child item planned into a sprint whose parent sits in another package may pass the one-package-per-sprint check; the roadmap report does not yet show the package count; the sources of the survey that gave the selection criteria were not opened. Guards read again: no scheduler or deadline was built (dates stay forecasts), no deployment tool was built, and no other lineage's records were changed." ;
    backlog:reportsOnObjective fw:Obj_RNP_Contain , fw:Obj_RNP_Count , fw:Obj_RNP_Coverage , fw:Obj_RNP_Guard_Deploying , fw:Obj_RNP_Guard_Others , fw:Obj_RNP_Guard_Planning , fw:Obj_RNP_Mission , fw:Obj_RNP_Readiness , fw:Obj_RNP_Roadmap , fw:Obj_RNP_Selection , fw:Obj_RNP_Sprint ;
    backlog:citesFinding fw:Find_RNP_ChildItemRefusedUnderEpic , fw:Find_RNP_ChildRefusedForParentDeliverable , fw:Find_RNP_CountCheckMissedUnplacedItems , fw:Find_RNP_DonePackageWithMissingStates , fw:Find_RNP_MixedSprintMissesChildOfOtherPackage , fw:Find_RNP_NoStageGateOnRoadmapCheck , fw:Find_RNP_PackageWithoutLineageLink , fw:Find_RNP_RoadmapNamedOtherLineagePackage , fw:Find_RNP_ViewDeliverableInconsistent ;
    backlog:statesBestPractice "Test a rule on a planted case and on a good case before releasing it, and have a fresh reviewer try the edges: each review of this lineage found a case the author had not." ,
        "A lineage cannot adopt a rule set after it opens: a rule born in a lineage binds the lineages that come after it, and the lineage that made it shows the pattern as a record, not as a bound lineage." .
