# ---- Lineage 29: second mission amendment, the general mission of governance (G224) ----
fw:Ruling_G224 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G224" ;
    rdfs:label "The Governance lineage's general mission is to govern the execution of a production lineage so that it can satisfy its mission"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The Owner proposed that the general mission of the Governance lineage is to govern, direct, monitor, control, correct and keep on track the execution of a production lineage, obeying its phases, connections, enforcements, ceremonies, methodologies, artifacts, dependencies, ordering, planning, predictions and task types, so that the production lineage can satisfy its mission, and that each production lineage adapts the general mission to its own. A fit-gap against the governance taxonomy of G217 corrected the proposal in three places: the satisfaction of the production lineage's mission is a benefit that appears later and is tracked, not a goal of this lineage; the amendment keeps the mission wording and the first amendment word for word, as G216 requires; and the subjects the proposal leaves out (accountability and roles, risk, assurance and truthful records, cost and speed of the run, benefits, closure and lessons) stay in the mission through the branches of G217." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner message of 2026-11-08 20:34 Istanbul (17:34 UTC): the general mission of the Governance lineage, to be adapted by each production lineage; build the goals for it." .
fw:MA2_ImpedimentsKnown a backlog:MissionAmendment ;
    rdfs:label "Mission amendment 2 of the Governance lineage: the execution of a production lineage is governed"@en ;
    backlog:amendsMission fw:Mission_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:amendedMissionStatement "An obstacle that stops or slows the work of a lineage can be named, recorded and cleared: it has a kind from a known set, each kind has the resolution methods known for it, it is recorded when it is met with the work it blocks, and its clearing records the method used, so that a blocked agent knows what to do next and the register can say why work ran late. Beside it, the lives of lineages are governed by known steps and checks that an agent follows without asking: how a lineage starts and is taken into work, how it is paused for an urgent interruption, how it is concluded and set down, and the facts kept about it. Beyond all this, the Governance lineage in general governs the execution of a production lineage so that the production lineage can satisfy its own mission: it governs, directs, monitors, controls and corrects the execution and keeps it on track, in every respect that the lineage's method names, namely the phases of the lineage and their order, the connections between its stages, the enforcements that check it, the ceremonies it follows, the methodologies it is run by, the artifacts it leaves, the dependencies and ordering of its work, its plans and predictions, and the types of its tasks. The mission of a production lineage is its own; each production lineage adapts this general mission to its mission, and whether the production lineage satisfies its mission is tracked as a benefit and is not claimed by this lineage." ;
    backlog:amendmentReason "The first amendment widened the mission to the lives of lineages (starting, pausing, concluding, the facts kept) with obstacles one branch. The Owner holds that the lineage is the general governance of a production lineage's execution, to be adapted by each production lineage. Fit-gap on 2026-11-08 of the Owner's proposal against the 21 areas of the scope and the thirteen-branch taxonomy of G217: the areas touch obstacles, lifecycle, records and closure, but none reaches methodologies, the order of phases, dependencies and ordering, plans and predictions, deployment, task types, or the cost and speed of the run; those are the subjects the goals of the next change request must answer." ;
    backlog:amendmentRuling fw:Ruling_G224 ;
    backlog:amendedBy backlog:Owner .
fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown rdfs:label "Governance lineage (Lineage 29): the execution of production lineages is governed; obstacles are one branch"@en .

# ---- Lineage 29: the scope grows to the general mission (G225) ----
fw:Ruling_G225 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G225" ;
    rdfs:label "A deployment is planned and marked by a milestone, time-box is a property of sprints and packages, and the Governance lineage organises the production lineage"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The Owner directed that deployment is decided by urgency, need, measures, business capability and impact; that after the packages, their content and sprint plans a deployment plan sets the package dependencies and the lineage objectives, and each deployment is marked with a milestone; that the box is renamed time-box, that a sprint is a time-box and packages should be time-boxed too, with time-box a property and the concepts that carry it obeying time-box rules; and that the Governance lineage, not the production lineage, adopts the package rules and organises the production lineage. These are the scope that the second mission amendment calls for." ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner messages of 2026-11-08 at 15:58 (deployment decision and plan with milestones) and 16:09 (time-box), Istanbul time." .
fw:CR_IK_General a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Grow the scope of the Governance lineage to its general mission: deployment planning, time-boxes and a governing link"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "The second mission amendment (G224) makes the lineage the general governance of a production lineage's execution. Fit-gap of 2026-11-08 against the 21 areas: phases and their order are covered by the order check and the stage digests (28 of 28 stage outputs carry a commit); methodologies are covered (2 of 2 lineages record their profile); task types are covered (26 of 26 tasks carry one); gaps stand in three places: 14 deployments mark no milestone, 15 packages carry no time-box, and the split of a started ungoverned lineage and the link from a production lineage to its governor are not expressible (five open questions of the 2SISA handover). Accountability, risk, assurance, cost and speed, benefits and closure lessons enter when taken up, as G217 says." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission4 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_IK_General a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of growing the scope of the Governance lineage to its general mission"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_IK_General ;
    backlog:affectsGoal fw:Goal_IK_Deploy , fw:Goal_IK_TimeBox , fw:Goal_IK_Governor ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Measured on 2026-11-08: the lineage had 50 stories and gains six, 56 in all, and the six added are placed in two new packages with five planned time-boxes; no area is added, so no stage is revised; three deliverables, three goals and three objectives are introduced and the stories are admitted. Paid for by time only: no item is removed." ;
    backlog:callsForItem fw:ST_IK_DeployPlan , fw:ST_IK_DeployMilestone , fw:ST_IK_TimeBoxProp , fw:ST_IK_TimeBoxRename , fw:ST_IK_GovernorLink , fw:ST_IK_SplitStarted .
fw:SC_IK_General a backlog:ScopeChange ; rdfs:label "Scope change of the Governance lineage: deployment planning, time-boxes and a governing link are admitted"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest fw:CR_IK_General ; backlog:changesScope fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "The Owner directed on 2026-11-08 (G224, G225): three deliverables under areas already held, three goals, three objectives and six stories. Paid for by time only: no item is removed." ;
    backlog:introducesElement fw:Del_IK_D48 , fw:Del_IK_D49 , fw:Del_IK_D50 , fw:Goal_IK_Deploy , fw:Goal_IK_TimeBox , fw:Goal_IK_Governor , fw:Obj_IK_Deploy , fw:Obj_IK_TimeBox , fw:Obj_IK_Governor ;
    backlog:admitsItem fw:ST_IK_DeployPlan ; backlog:admitsItem fw:ST_IK_DeployMilestone ; backlog:admitsItem fw:ST_IK_TimeBoxProp ; backlog:admitsItem fw:ST_IK_TimeBoxRename ; backlog:admitsItem fw:ST_IK_GovernorLink ; backlog:admitsItem fw:ST_IK_SplitStarted .
fw:Del_IK_D48 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "48.1 A deployment of a package is planned: the plan states why it ships now (urgency, need, measures, business capability, impact), which packages it follows and which objectives of the lineage it moves, it is marked by a milestone, and the register derives the state of the milestone from what was deployed"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_IK_Tools ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "it governs, directs, monitors, controls and corrects the execution and keeps it on track" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown .
fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:requiresDeliverable fw:Del_IK_D48 .
fw:Del_IK_D49 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "49.1 A time-box is a property that sprints and packages carry, with a start and an end that are forecasts only, and the concepts that carry it obey stated rules; the box tool and its words are renamed the time-box tool"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_IK_Tools ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "its plans and predictions" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown .
fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:requiresDeliverable fw:Del_IK_D49 .
fw:Del_IK_D50 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "50.1 A lineage names the lineage that governs it, a governing lineage organises a production lineage by a typed link, and a started lineage that was not governed is split into a governing and a production lineage with its record kept and no Abandoned outcome"@en ;
    backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_IK_MissionChange ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "each production lineage adapts this general mission to its mission" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown .
fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:requiresDeliverable fw:Del_IK_D50 .
