# ---- Lineage 29, box 39 (G227): the lineage role, the governing link and the rule set that binds them ----
backlog:LR_Governance a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:LineageRole ; rdfs:label "Governance"@en ;
    skos:definition "The lineage organises and watches the lives of production lineages: how they run, what blocks them, how they are timed and measured. It governs production lineages by the link governsLineage and builds no product of its own beyond its method."@en .
backlog:LR_Production a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:LineageRole ; rdfs:label "Production"@en ;
    skos:definition "The lineage builds a product or a deliverable for the Owner and is organised by one governance lineage."@en .
backlog:RS_GovernanceRequired a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:RuleSet ;
    rdfs:label "Every lineage has a role, and a governance lineage governs production lineages by a typed link (G227)"@en ;
    skos:definition "A lineage that adopts it states whether it is a governance lineage or a production lineage; a governing link joins a governance lineage to a production lineage and never a lineage to itself; a production lineage is governed by at most one governance lineage and names it; a governance lineage governs at least one production lineage and, when opened under profile revision 17 or later, adopts the rule set. A RuleSet: the duty to state a role and the duty of a governance lineage to govern at least one production lineage bind only lineages that adopt it (lineages opened earlier are not bound, and adopt it by a stage revision), while the checks on one role, the link between roles, one governor, a production lineage naming its governor and a governance lineage adopting the rule set apply to every lineage that states a role or a link, the last only from profile revision 17 on or where no revision is stated."@en .
backlog:Pr_17 a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:ProfileRevision ; rdfs:label "Profile revision 17"@en ; backlog:revisionNumber 17 ; skos:definition "Adds to the agentic adaptive profile (AAL) the rule set that every lineage states its role and that a governance lineage governs production lineages by a typed link, so that parallel sessions can build their governance lineages in one form. The other profiles are not changed."@en .
backlog:Profile_AgenticAdaptive backlog:profileIncludes backlog:RS_GovernanceRequired .
backlog:RS_GovernanceRequired backlog:introducedInRevision backlog:Pr_17 .
fw:Ruling_G227 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G227" ;
    rdfs:label "A lineage has a role, governance or production, and a governance lineage governs production lineages by one typed link"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The Owner directed on 2026-11-09 that the formal role of a governing lineage and the duality of lineages are set in the BRSF corpus at once, so that parallel sessions can build their governance lineages. Every lineage holds at most one role (hasLineageRole: governance or production) and a governing link (governsLineage) runs only from a governance lineage to a production lineage and never to itself; a production lineage has at most one governor. These checks apply to every lineage that states a role or a link, adopting or not: one role, the link between roles, one governor, and a production lineage names its governor. A lineage that adopts RS_GovernanceRequired states its role; a governance lineage among them governs at least one production lineage; a lineage with the governance role that was opened under profile revision 17 or later, or states no revision, adopts the rule set. AAL includes the rule set from profile revision 17, so a lineage opened under it adopts it by G155. What the criteria cannot reach: a lineage opened earlier cannot adopt a rule set after opening (G89), so the Governance lineage (Lineage 29) states its role and governs Lineage 32 but is only advised by a warning to adopt the rule set, until a later stage revision (G192) does it. DEPARTURE FROM THE CRITERIA AS WRITTEN, for the Owner to accept or reject: the criterion that a governance lineage adopts the rule set is a refusal only for lineages opened under revision 17 or later or stating no revision; for the Governance lineage it is a warning, because a lineage cannot adopt a rule set after opening (G89) and the route is a stage revision, which for this lineage rebuilds the Backlog stage, as the fifth stage revision did for the package rules (G192 applied by precedent, not a new rule). A second departure: a lineage that states no role and adopts nothing escapes every governance check, so the duty to state a role binds only adopting lineages. The rules that need adoption do not yet bind a real lineage; the one real link is checked by the checks that apply to every lineage."@en ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:LineageRoleStatedShape , backlog:GoverningLinkRolesShape , backlog:OneGovernorShape , backlog:OneRoleShape , backlog:ProductionNamesGovernorShape , backlog:GovernanceNamesProductionShape , backlog:GovernanceRoleBoundShape , backlog:GovernanceRoleBoundEarlierShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner message of 2026-11-09 at 09:07 Istanbul time (the formal governing-lineage role and the lineage duality are urgent); G226." .
fw:Ruling_G227 backlog:rulingDecides backlog:RS_GovernanceRequired , backlog:Pr_17 , backlog:Profile_AgenticAdaptive .
fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown backlog:hasLineageRole backlog:LR_Governance ; backlog:governsLineage fw:L_RoadmapNeedsPackages .
fw:L_RoadmapNeedsPackages backlog:hasLineageRole backlog:LR_Production .
