# ---- Lineage 29: an epic is a backlog item groomed into stories (G228) ----
fw:Ruling_G228 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G228" ;
    rdfs:label "An epic is a backlog item that describes a feature of the final product at high level; it is groomed into stories before packages and sprints are made, and it is not asked for a package or a score and holds no lineage open itself"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The Owner ruled on 2026-11-09 at 15:26 that an epic is a product backlog item and needs no closure: the idea of closing an epic is a legacy misreading that treated an epic as a development subject. An epic's only mission is to define a specific feature of the final product at high level; it is groomed into stories, to understand its scope and its business value, before it is taken into a plan. The order the Owner set for the IPage lineage on 2026-11-09 at 13:55 is the same: epics are defined from the scope, groomed into stories, packages are chosen from the groomed items, and sprints are planned to the packages. In the rules this means: a lineage that adopts RS_PackagesRequired no longer asks an epic for a package, a priority score or an impact (the stories carry them), refuses an epic that is a member of a package, and three other rules no longer bind an epic: that a parent whose children are finished is Done, that an open unscored item is a silent gap, and that a lineage recorded Achieved has no open item (for an epic that has stories, the stories hold the lineage open; an epic with no stories still does). Nothing refuses a score placed on an epic unless its stories are also scored (the parent-score rule, unchanged). An item typed both as an epic and as a story is treated as an epic. Which stage holds the grooming is NOT settled here: the Owner\'s words of 13:55 put it in the roadmap stage, before packages are chosen, while the package rules ask for packages from the Backlog stage on (RNP_LINEAGE_NOPKG, unchanged); the Owner is asked to settle it. Not changed, and held for the next change request of the Governance lineage: the package-count tool still counts an epic as an item. Not changed: an epic that decomposes into nothing is still refused (L4), an epic is still refused in an iteration or a deployment unit, and an epic still carries its Definition of Done before it decomposes (L3). Also corrected by this ruling, as vocabulary errors found on the way: reach, impact, confidence and effort may stand on any work item as well as on a score, and the text of a checkpoint no longer says that a condition and a date exclude each other when the date is a forecast."@en ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape , backlog:EpicNotInPackageShape , backlog:ItemInPackageShape , backlog:ItemSelectionValuesShape , backlog:DecompositionStateAgreesShape , backlog:SilentGapShape , backlog:LineageClosureCompleteShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner message of 2026-11-09 at 15:26 Istanbul time; the Owner's order for the IPage lineage of 2026-11-09 at 13:55, relayed by the IPage handover on the groomed epic in a package." .
fw:CR_IK_Epic a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Treat an epic as a backlog item that is groomed into stories, with no package, no score and no closure of its own"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Routed under the discipline as work that serves the live mission (route a). Two rules of the framework contradict each other on a groomed epic: the package rules ask the epic for a package and a score, and the parent-score rule forbids a score on a parent whose children are scored. The IPage lineage met it on six epics and its Backlog stage is blocked. The Owner ruled that an epic is a backlog item that is groomed, not a development subject." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission4 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_IK_Epic a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of treating an epic as a groomed backlog item"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_IK_Epic ;
    backlog:affectsGoal fw:Goal_IK_Epic ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Measured on 2026-11-09: the lineage holds 57 stories and no epic; one story is added, in a new package that delivers one new deliverable. Paid for by time only: no item is removed. Reaches the package rules (RS_PackagesRequired) and the rule that derives the state of a parent from its children; lineages that adopt them and hold epics are freed from an impossible record." ;
    backlog:callsForItem fw:ST_IK_EpicGroomed .
fw:SC_IK_Epic a backlog:ScopeChange ; rdfs:label "Scope change of the Governance lineage: an epic is a groomed backlog item"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest fw:CR_IK_Epic ; backlog:changesScope fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "The Owner ruled on 2026-11-09 (G228) that an epic is a backlog item that is groomed: one deliverable, one goal, one objective and one story. Paid for by time only: no item is removed." ;
    backlog:introducesElement fw:Del_IK_D52 , fw:Goal_IK_Epic , fw:Obj_IK_Epic ;
    backlog:admitsItem fw:ST_IK_EpicGroomed .
fw:Ruling_G228 backlog:rulingDecides fw:CR_IK_Epic .
