# ---- Lineage 29: the score of an epic and the timing of packages (G229) ----
backlog:Method_RollUp a owl:NamedIndividual , backlog:PrioritizationMethod ;
    rdfs:label "Roll-up of the stories' scores"@en ;
    skos:definition "The score of an epic is collected from the scores of its children: the effort-weighted mean of the scores of the children that carry a score and an effort, that is the sum of each child's score times its effort divided by the sum of their efforts. The children\'s scores counted are those that no other score replaces, and a child whose effort is not above zero is left out; used after a grooming step; nothing is added on top of the children's scores, so no value is counted twice."@en ;
    dcterms:source "The Owner's proposal of 2026-11-09 at 16:52 (an epic is valued before grooming, then collected from its stories); the weighting by effort is the framework's choice, so that the roll-up of RICE scores is again value over cost."@en .
fw:Ruling_G229 a backlog:GovernanceRuling ;
    backlog:hasRulingIdentifier "G229" ;
    rdfs:label "An epic carries an estimated score that its stories' scores replace; packages are asked for once development is ongoing"@en ;
    backlog:hasRulingStatement "The Owner proposed on 2026-11-09 at 16:52 and confirmed at 16:57 (relayed by the IPage handover on the score of a groomed epic): a value is assigned to an epic before grooming, and after that the valuations of its stories are collected to finalise the epic's priority score; if grooming takes steps, the epic is updated at the end of each step. He ruled at 18:00 that packages are subject of planning, can only be defined after the backlog is groomed, can be presented before the roadmap as an ingredient of it, can sit directly in the backlog when the work is already groomed and scoped (as a heritage of a legacy or earlier lineage), and can even come after the roadmap, because grooming goes on as lower-priority work comes into focus; this is why the lineage is flexible and not step-bound. In the rules: a score names the score it replaces (replacesScore) and a score that is replaced is not live, so the old one stays visible and only the newest counts; a roll-up method (Method_RollUp) exists, and an epic's live score may be made by it beside scored stories, with a check that its value equals the roll-up of the stories that carry a score and an effort at that moment (within 0.01); an epic whose live score is not a roll-up is still refused beside scored stories (the parent-score rule), and so is a roll-up score on a parent that is not an epic; only a score of a child that no other score replaces, and only a child with an effort above zero, counts in the roll-up; a score may replace only an earlier score of the same item that is on an item itself, and two scores may not replace each other; the date order is checked only when both scores are dated; a partly groomed epic is rolled up from the stories scored so far and is replaced again at the next grooming step. The package rules bind a lineage from the status In progress, not from the Backlog stage, and a backlog item that is still Proposed (not groomed) is not asked for a package. The package-count tool no longer lists an epic or an item still Proposed as unplaced. Not enforced, and not claimed: that a package holds only groomed items, that a roll-up is made at a grooming step (it is compared with the stories at validation time, so it is refused after a story is re-scored until it is replaced), and that the estimate before grooming is labelled; a partly groomed epic is rolled up from the scored stories only, so a single scored story among many gives the epic that story\'s score. Not changed: a package delivers deliverables, the rule that a sprint plans only items of a package, and the other checks of an epic (G228). The method of the roll-up, and the reading of a partly groomed epic, are the framework\'s choice where the Owner gave none: the Owner is asked to accept or reject them."@en ;
    backlog:enforcedByShape backlog:OwnerRulingDatedShape , backlog:EpicRollUpAgreesShape , backlog:ScoreReplacedNotLiveShape , backlog:ItemInPackageShape , backlog:LineageHasPackageShape , backlog:RoadmapNamesPackageShape , backlog:DeliverableDeliveredShape , backlog:ItemInOnePackageShape , backlog:ItemSelectionValuesShape , backlog:ItemDependsForwardShape ;
    backlog:rulingSource "Owner messages of 2026-11-09 at 16:52 and 16:57 (relayed by the IPage handover on the score of a groomed epic) and at 18:00 Istanbul time (timing of packages)." .
fw:CR_IK_Epic2 a backlog:ChangeRequest ; rdfs:label "Let an epic carry an estimated score that its stories' scores replace, and ask for packages once development is ongoing"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Routed under the discipline as work that serves the live mission (route a), and as the part of the Owner's epic ruling that release 5.5.12 left open. The IPage lineage cannot groom its epics into scored stories: the parent-score rule refuses a score on an epic beside scored stories and the one-live-score rule gives no way to replace one; and the package rules ask for packages as soon as the Backlog stage is reached, which the Owner says is too early." ;
    backlog:supportsObjective fw:Obj_IK_Mission4 ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
fw:IA_IK_Epic2 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; rdfs:label "Impact of the epic score and the timing of packages"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest fw:CR_IK_Epic2 ;
    backlog:affectsGoal fw:Goal_IK_Epic2 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Measured on 2026-11-09: the lineage holds 58 stories and no epic; one story is added, in a new package that delivers one new deliverable. Paid for by time only: no item is removed. Loosens the package rules for lineages that adopt them (they bind from the status In progress), and lets an epic carry a rolled-up score." ;
    backlog:callsForItem fw:ST_IK_EpicScore .
fw:SC_IK_Epic2 a backlog:ScopeChange ; rdfs:label "Scope change of the Governance lineage: the score of an epic and the timing of packages"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest fw:CR_IK_Epic2 ; backlog:changesScope fw:Scope4_ImpedimentsKnown ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "The Owner ruled on 2026-11-09 (G229): one deliverable, one goal, one objective and one story. Paid for by time only: no item is removed." ;
    backlog:introducesElement fw:Del_IK_D53 , fw:Goal_IK_Epic2 , fw:Obj_IK_Epic2 ;
    backlog:admitsItem fw:ST_IK_EpicScore .
fw:Ruling_G229 backlog:rulingDecides fw:CR_IK_Epic2 .
