fw:Ev_IK_EpicScore a backlog:TestEvidence ; rdfs:label "The check for story EpicScore"@en ;
    backlog:evidenceVerified true ; backlog:hasTestId "EpicScore" ;
    backlog:hasTestSpec "02-shacl-safeguards/backlog_shacl_v1_219_0.ttl" ;
    backlog:attestsCriterion fw:AC_IK_EpicScore ;
    backlog:hasVerificationMethod "A score can name the score it replaces (the old one stays, not live); a roll-up method exists, and an epic's live roll-up score may stand beside scored stories if it equals the effort-weighted mean of the live scores of its stories that carry an effort above zero; a roll-up on a parent that is not an epic, a replacer on no item, a score of another item and two scores replacing each other are refused. The package rules bind from the status In progress instead of the Backlog stage, an item still Proposed is not asked for a package, and the package-count tool no longer lists an epic or a Proposed item as unplaced." ;
    backlog:verifiedAt "2026-11-09T15:41:20Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:verifiedByTool "backlog_validate v1.19.0 with the changed shapes (vocabulary v1.178.0, fixture v1.77.0); package-count tool v1.2.0 and its probe" ;
    backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "02-shacl-safeguards/backlog_shacl_v1_219_0.ttl" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_ImpedimentsKnown .
fw:AC_IK_EpicScore backlog:satisfiedByArtifact "02-shacl-safeguards/backlog_shacl_v1_219_0.ttl" .
fw:H_IK_EpicScore a backlog:TestHarness ; rdfs:label "Harness for story EpicScore"@en ;
    backlog:harnessFor fw:ST_IK_EpicScore ; backlog:hasHarnessEvidence fw:Ev_IK_EpicScore ; backlog:harnessComplete true ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Each new check has a bad fixture case that fires and good cases stay quiet (an estimate replaced by a right roll-up, a re-scored story, a zero-effort story left out, a lineage at the Backlog stage with no package); the old package cases moved to In progress still fire; the package-count probe passes; two independent reviews read the work, the second accepting it." .
fw:Demo_IK_EpicScore a backlog:DemoRun ; backlog:hasWorkKind backlog:WorkKind_Control ; backlog:demonstratesItem fw:ST_IK_EpicScore ; backlog:demonstratedAgainst fw:AC_IK_EpicScore ; backlog:demoAt "2026-11-09T15:41:21Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:hasDemoShown "The fixture run shows ROLLUP_BAD, SCORE_REPLACE and the parent-score refusal of a roll-up on a non-epic parent each firing on their cases and none on the good cases." ;
    backlog:hasDemoResult "An epic can be valued before grooming and its score replaced by a roll-up of its stories without any rule contradicting another, and packages are asked for once development is ongoing. Not enforced: that a package holds only groomed items, that a roll-up is made at a grooming step. Three small points found by the last review stay open: a story with two live scores of different methods is counted twice in a roll-up, a cycle of three undated replacements draws no message, and a roll-up score on a parent with no scored children is not caught." .
