fw:Find_IK_RulesMetAtFirstRealUse a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem fw:ST_IK_EpicScore ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The score rules, the one-live-score rule and the package rules were each made for a record that never changed; the Owner's description of an epic's life (valued, groomed, re-valued) met all three at once only when a real lineage tried it, and the first version of the roll-up again counted replaced scores and exempted every parent." ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Applied: a replaced score is not live, the roll-up reads live scores only, the exemption is for epics only, and every new check has its own case. Open: a step that tries new rules together with the older ones on a register that holds the kinds of items they bind, before a release; and the three small points of the last review." .
